//
// Created     : 2026-08-30 (Military date format - Year-Month-Day)
//
// Description : Finds package files that exist in more than one place under the workspace, and
//               says which copy the compiler actually used.
//
//               A stale copy compiles perfectly, which is the whole problem: fix the library and
//               the workspace keeps building the old file. One real case drove this - a workspace
//               carried nine copies of the same wrapper package; the modernised one was a declared
//               git dependency and checked out, yet a vendored copy inside ANOTHER package won the
//               search path, so seven obsolete-function warnings survived every attempt to fix
//               them at the source. Nothing in the compiler output says "you have another copy".
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use GlobalFunctionsProcedures.pkg
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use RefactorFileIO.pkg           // rfOpenOutput / rfCloseOutput / rfFileSearchRecursive

// The file that picks the language DataFlex's own texts compile in (see IsLanguageSettingLeaf).
Define CS_LanguageSettingFile for "Language_Current.inc"

/* ---- WHICH COPY THE BUILD COMPILED - the note on a dashboard finding row (Nils 2026-09-11) ----

   Nils, of a row about a file that exists twice under the workspace: "It is the '2 copies of this
   file exist here...' that is very confusing". The note these replace counted FILE NAMES under the
   home and printed "N copies of this file exist here; the build uses THIS one" on every row whose
   name was counted twice. The other copy sat in a language-variant folder no build searches,
   nothing said where it was, and "THIS one" was never checked - a row about that other copy would
   have printed the same sentence, falsely.

   The build's own listing records which file it compiled ("Including file:"), so the note is
   decided from that: a row about the copy the build compiled needs no note; a row about a
   DIFFERENT file of a compiled name gets the compiled copy named - the one case where the reader
   is about to edit something the compiler never reads; anything else, no note.

   Pure and global. The dashboard asks once per finding row, where creating an object costs and
   copying an array per row once cost a 131-second render (see CompiledScopeStamp). The index is
   built ONCE per listing; a row then pays one BinarySearchArray and a string compare. Defined in
   calling order - a function used in an expression must already be known to the compiler. */

// The file part of a path, lowercased - the one spelling the index and every lookup share.
Function FileLeafLower Global String sPath Returns String
    Integer iAt

    Move (Replaces("/", Trim(sPath), "\")) to sPath
    Move (RightPos("\", sPath)) to iAt
    If (iAt > 0) ;
        Move (Right(sPath, (Length(sPath) - iAt))) to sPath
    Function_Return (Lowercase(sPath))
End_Function

/* THE PACKAGE CHECKOUT A FILE SITS IN (2026-11-12): the folder that holds it, with its trailing "\" -
   "E:\Ws\DfPkg\NilsSve_VDFQuery20-904dc8c\" - for a file in either of df-cli's two pools,
   <workspace>\DfPkg\<checkout>\ and ...\DataFlex\Packages\Cache\<entry>\; "" for any other file, and for
   one directly in the pool root, which is in no package. FailingPackageCopies counts errors per package
   with it. The same two shapes as PoolPackageDisplayNameOf below. */
Function PoolPackageRootOf Global String sFile Returns String
    String sLow sSeg
    Integer iPos iEnd

    Move (Replaces("/", Trim(sFile), "\")) to sFile
    Move (Lowercase(sFile)) to sLow
    Move (Pos("\dfpkg\", sLow)) to iPos
    If (iPos > 0) ;
        Move (iPos + 7) to iPos
    Else Begin
        Move (Pos("\dataflex\packages\cache\", sLow)) to iPos
        If (iPos = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (iPos + 25) to iPos
    End
    Move (Mid(sFile, (Length(sFile)), iPos)) to sSeg
    Move (Pos("\", sSeg)) to iEnd
    If (iEnd = 0) ;
        Function_Return ""
    Function_Return (Left(sFile, (iPos + iEnd - 1)))
End_Function

/* THE PACKAGE A POOL FILE BELONGS TO, as the name a reader knows it by - "VDFQuery20". Moved here from
   cModAnalyzer.PoolPackageDisplayName on 2026-11-12 (that method now returns this), so the "In packages"
   band and the overriding-copies rows can never name one package two ways. See that method's comment
   for the two pool shapes and the tail rule. PURE. */
Function PoolPackageDisplayNameOf Global String sFile Returns String
    String sLow sSeg sTail sCh
    Integer iPos iEnd i iLen
    Boolean bHexOrVer

    Move (Lowercase(sFile)) to sLow
    Move (Pos("\dfpkg\", sLow)) to iPos
    If (iPos > 0) ;
        Move (iPos + 7) to iPos
    Else Begin
        Move (Pos("\dataflex\packages\cache\", sLow)) to iPos
        If (iPos = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (iPos + 25) to iPos
    End
    Move (Mid(sFile, (Length(sFile)), iPos)) to sSeg
    Move (Pos("\", sSeg)) to iEnd
    If (iEnd = 0) ;
        Function_Return ""              // a file directly in the pool root is not a package
    Move (Left(sSeg, (iEnd - 1))) to sSeg
    // <Owner>_<Name>: the first underscore is df-cli's separator.
    Move (Pos("_", sSeg)) to iPos
    If (iPos > 0 and iPos < Length(sSeg)) ;
        Move (Mid(sSeg, Length(sSeg), (iPos + 1))) to sSeg
    // -<commit> / -<version> tail: strip only when it really looks like one.
    Move (RightPos("-", sSeg)) to iPos
    If (iPos > 1 and iPos < Length(sSeg)) Begin
        Move (Mid(sSeg, Length(sSeg), (iPos + 1))) to sTail
        Move (Length(sTail)) to iLen
        Move True to bHexOrVer
        For i from 1 to iLen
            Move (Lowercase(Mid(sTail, 1, i))) to sCh
            If (not("0123456789abcdef" contains sCh)) ;
                Move False to bHexOrVer
        Loop
        If (bHexOrVer = True and iLen < 7) ;
            Move False to bHexOrVer     // too short for a commit - "Utils-2" style names keep their tail... unless it is a version
        If (bHexOrVer = False) Begin
            // A dotted version tail ("1.2.0")?
            Move True to bHexOrVer
            For i from 1 to iLen
                Move (Mid(sTail, 1, i)) to sCh
                If (not("0123456789." contains sCh)) ;
                    Move False to bHexOrVer
            Loop
            If (not(sTail contains ".")) ;
                Move False to bHexOrVer
        End
        If (bHexOrVer = True) ;
            Move (Left(sSeg, (iPos - 1))) to sSeg
    End
    Function_Return sSeg
End_Function

/* The listing's compiled files as a lookup. Returns the distinct file names, lowercased and SORTED
   for BinarySearchArray, and fills asBuilt at the same indexes with the path compiled under each -
   Character(9)-separated in the rare case the build compiled two files of one name, which a Use
   naming a relative path can do. */
Function CompiledLeafIndex Global String[] asCompiled String[] ByRef asBuilt Returns String[]
    String[] asAll asLeaf
    String sPath sLow
    Integer i iMax iAt

    Move (SizeOfArray(asCompiled) - 1) to iMax
    For i from 0 to iMax
        If (Trim(asCompiled[i]) <> "") ;
            Move (FileLeafLower(asCompiled[i])) to asAll[SizeOfArray(asAll)]
    Loop
    Move (SortArray(asAll)) to asAll
    // Adjacent duplicates out. i = 0 is its own branch: DataFlex does not short-circuit, so
    // "i = 0 or asAll[i] <> asAll[i - 1]" would still read asAll[-1].
    Move (SizeOfArray(asAll) - 1) to iMax
    For i from 0 to iMax
        If (i = 0) ;
            Move asAll[i] to asLeaf[SizeOfArray(asLeaf)]
        Else If (asAll[i] <> asAll[i - 1]) ;
            Move asAll[i] to asLeaf[SizeOfArray(asLeaf)]
    Loop
    Move (ResizeArray(asBuilt, SizeOfArray(asLeaf))) to asBuilt
    Move (SizeOfArray(asCompiled) - 1) to iMax
    For i from 0 to iMax
        Move (Trim(asCompiled[i])) to sPath
        If (sPath <> "") Begin
            Move (BinarySearchArray(FileLeafLower(sPath), asLeaf)) to iAt
            If (iAt <> -1) Begin
                Move (Lowercase(sPath)) to sLow
                If (asBuilt[iAt] = "") ;
                    Move sPath to asBuilt[iAt]
                Else If (Pos((Character(9) + sLow + Character(9)), (Character(9) + Lowercase(asBuilt[iAt]) + Character(9))) = 0) ;
                    Move (asBuilt[iAt] + Character(9) + sPath) to asBuilt[iAt]
            End
        End
    Loop
    Function_Return asLeaf
End_Function

/* The compiled copy to name on a row about sFile, given sBuilt - the path(s) the build compiled
   under sFile's name, as CompiledLeafIndex stores them. "" when sFile IS one of them - the row is
   about the copy the build read, and there is nothing to warn about - or when there is none. */
Function CompiledCopyFor Global String sFile String sBuilt Returns String
    String sLow
    Integer iTab

    Move (Lowercase(Trim(sFile))) to sLow
    If (sLow = "" or Trim(sBuilt) = "") ;
        Function_Return ""
    If (Pos((Character(9) + sLow + Character(9)), (Character(9) + Lowercase(sBuilt) + Character(9))) > 0) ;
        Function_Return ""
    Move (Pos(Character(9), sBuilt)) to iTab
    If (iTab > 0) ;
        Function_Return (Left(sBuilt, (iTab - 1)))
    Function_Return sBuilt
End_Function

// The program a listing is for: "<name>.x64.prn" or "<name>.prn" -> "<name>.src"; "" otherwise.
Function ProgramOfListing Global String sPrn Returns String
    String sLeaf
    Integer iAt

    Move (Trim(sPrn)) to sLeaf
    Move (RightPos("\", sLeaf)) to iAt
    If (iAt > 0) ;
        Move (Right(sLeaf, (Length(sLeaf) - iAt))) to sLeaf
    If (Lowercase(Right(sLeaf, 4)) <> ".prn") ;
        Function_Return ""
    Move (Left(sLeaf, (Length(sLeaf) - 4))) to sLeaf
    If (Lowercase(Right(sLeaf, 4)) = ".x64" or Lowercase(Right(sLeaf, 4)) = ".x86") ;
        Move (Left(sLeaf, (Length(sLeaf) - 4))) to sLeaf
    If (sLeaf = "") ;
        Function_Return ""
    Function_Return (sLeaf + ".src")
End_Function

/* The note's words: "<program> compiles <copy>, not this copy. " - the compiled copy relative to the
   workspace home when it lies inside it, so it fits the cell the note leads. A folder that merely
   STARTS like the home is not inside it. Plain text: it goes through a tooltip builder that
   escapes. */
Function CompiledElsewhereNote Global String sProgram String sBuilt String sHome Returns String
    String sShow sHomeSep

    Move (Trim(sBuilt)) to sShow
    If (sShow = "") ;
        Function_Return ""
    Move (Trim(sHome)) to sHomeSep
    If (sHomeSep <> "" and Right(sHomeSep, 1) <> "\") ;
        Move (sHomeSep + "\") to sHomeSep
    If (sHomeSep <> "" and Lowercase(Left(sShow, Length(sHomeSep))) = Lowercase(sHomeSep)) ;
        Move (Right(sShow, (Length(sShow) - Length(sHomeSep)))) to sShow
    If (Trim(sProgram) = "") ;
        Function_Return ("The last build compiled " + sShow + ", not this copy. ")
    Function_Return (Trim(sProgram) + " compiles " + sShow + ", not this copy. ")
End_Function

Class cShadowedPackageFiles is a cObject

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
        // The report this run wrote, for the caller's "Other Log Files" list.
        Property String psLogFile ""
        // Test-only override for KeptShadowsJsonPath - see the note there. "" in production.
        Property String psKeptShadowsFile ""
        // The listing the resolution evidence came from - named in the report so the reader can
        // tell WHICH compile is being described.
        Property String psListingUsed ""
    End_Procedure

    /* PURE. One listing record, of the shape the compiler writes into a .prn:

           Including file: vWin32fh.pkg    (E:\Ws\DfPkg\SomePackage-<sha>\AppSrc\vWin32fh.pkg)

       Returns the LOWERCASE leaf name and fills sPath with the full path exactly as written; ""
       when the line is not an include record.

       The first "(" is the wrapper's, never one inside the path: a path may well contain
       "Program Files (x86)", but that sits AFTER the opening one, and the close is taken from the
       RIGHT. A file NAME containing a parenthesis would break this, and no package has one. */
    Function IncludedFileFromPrnLine String sLine String ByRef sPath Returns String
        String  sTrim sRest sName
        Integer iOpen iClose

        Move "" to sPath
        Move (Trim(sLine)) to sTrim
        If (Lowercase(Left(sTrim, 15)) <> "including file:") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Trim(Right(sTrim, (Length(sTrim) - 15)))) to sRest
        Move (Pos("(", sRest))      to iOpen
        Move (RightPos(")", sRest)) to iClose
        If (iOpen = 0 or iClose <= iOpen) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Trim(Mid(sRest, (iClose - iOpen - 1), (iOpen + 1)))) to sPath
        Move (Trim(Left(sRest, (iOpen - 1)))) to sName
        If (sName = "" or sPath = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (Lowercase(sName))
    End_Function

    // PURE. Every candidate that shares sLeaf with sWinner but is not sWinner itself - the copies
    // the compile did NOT use. Case-insensitive on the leaf and on the whole path, because Windows
    // hides filename case and the two records reach us from different sources.
    Function ShadowCopiesOf String sLeaf String sWinner String[] asCandidates Returns String[]
        String[] asOut
        String   sWinLC sLeafLC sCand
        Integer  i iLast

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sWinner))) to sWinLC
        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sLeaf)))   to sLeafLC
        Move (SizeOfArray(asCandidates) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Trim(asCandidates[i])) to sCand
            If (sCand <> "") Begin
                If (Lowercase(ExtractFileName(sCand)) = sLeafLC) Begin
                    If (Lowercase(sCand) <> sWinLC) ;
                        Move sCand to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    /* The compiler listing to read the resolution out of - the NEWEST .prn under the workspace.

       Newest rather than "the main program's", because the resolution recorded in a listing is
       only true of the build that wrote it: an older listing describes a path layout that may
       since have changed. "" when the workspace has never been compiled, which the caller reports
       rather than guessing a winner from path order. */
    Function NewestListingFile String sHome Returns String
        tRFSearchResult[] aFound
        String   sBest
        DateTime dtBest dtThis
        Integer  i iLast

        Move "" to sBest
        Move (rfFileSearchRecursive((vFolderFormat(sHome) + "*.prn"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFound
        Move (SizeOfArray(aFound) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move aFound[i].dtLastWriteDateTime to dtThis
            If (sBest = "" or dtThis > dtBest) Begin
                Move aFound[i].sFilename to sBest
                Move dtThis to dtBest
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return sBest
    End_Function

    /* PURE. The extensions a Use or an #INCLUDE resolves by NAME through the search path - the
       files the sweeps and both reference sets are built from.

       WIDENED 2026-09-15 from .pkg / .inc / .h, and the earlier reasoning is worth keeping because
       it was half right: a workspace's OWN .vw / .dd / .sl is reached by its own path, so a
       same-named one in a variant folder is a different screen, not a shadow. What that missed is
       the other half of the population. The install ships .dg / .vw / .mac (MonthCalendarPrompt.dg
       among them), and libraries ship .utl / .nui / .vw - one migration copy carried the app's own
       DATES.UTL and MACROS.UTL in front of VDFQuery's, invisible to a three-extension sweep. Which
       copy is a shadow is decided by the LISTING, not by the extension; the sweep's only job is to
       find every file a Use could reach. .src stays out: a program is never Used, and a library's
       sample program beside the app's own of the same name is not a copy of anything. */
    Function SourceLeafExtensions Returns String[]
        String[] asOut
        Move ".pkg" to asOut[0]
        Move ".inc" to asOut[1]
        Move ".h"   to asOut[2]
        Move ".utl" to asOut[3]
        Move ".nui" to asOut[4]
        Move ".dg"  to asOut[5]
        Move ".vw"  to asOut[6]
        Move ".sl"  to asOut[7]
        Move ".dd"  to asOut[8]
        Move ".rv"  to asOut[9]
        Move ".bp"  to asOut[10]
        Move ".wo"  to asOut[11]
        Move ".cls" to asOut[12]
        Move ".mac" to asOut[13]
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // Every source file under the workspace (SourceLeafExtensions), full paths.
    Function WorkspaceSourceFiles String sHome Returns String[]
        tRFSearchResult[] aFound
        String[] asExt asOut
        String   sPath sSkip
        Integer  iMask iMaskLast iFile iLast

        // OUR OWN BACKUP TREE IS NOT A SHADOW. DFRefactor mirrors the files it changes into
        // DFRefactor_Backup\<drive>\<path>, so every backed-up file matched its own original and
        // came back as a finding - 17 of the first live run's 53, every one of them noise, and
        // noise of the worst kind: the tool reporting itself (Nils 2026-08-30).
        Move (Lowercase(CS_DirSeparator + CS_BackupFolder + CS_DirSeparator)) to sSkip
        Get SourceLeafExtensions to asExt
        Move (SizeOfArray(asExt) - 1) to iMaskLast
        For iMask from 0 to iMaskLast
            Move (rfFileSearchRecursive((vFolderFormat(sHome) + "*" + asExt[iMask]), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFound
            Move (SizeOfArray(aFound) - 1) to iLast
            For iFile from 0 to iLast
                Move (Trim(aFound[iFile].sFilename)) to sPath
                If (sPath <> "") Begin
                    If (not(Lowercase(sPath) contains sSkip)) ;
                        Move sPath to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
                End
            Loop
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // PURE. A folder name reduced to letters and digits, lowercased - so "Data Folder Selector"
    // and "NilsSve_DataFolderSelector_Library_DF26-40f317da" can be recognised as the same library
    // under two naming conventions.
    Function NormalisedFolderName String sName Returns String
        String  sOut sCh
        Integer i iLen

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sName))) to sOut
        Move (Length(sOut)) to iLen
        Move "" to sName
        For i from 1 to iLen
            Move (Mid(sOut, 1, i)) to sCh
            If ((sCh >= "a" and sCh <= "z") or (sCh >= "0" and sCh <= "9")) ;
                Move (sName + sCh) to sName
        Loop
        Function_Return sName
    End_Function

    /* The DfPkg package checkout that corresponds to a Libraries\ folder, or "".

       Matched on the normalised name being CONTAINED in the package's: a checkout is named
       <owner>_<library>-<sha>, so the library's own name is a fragment of it. Deliberately not the
       reverse - "duf" must find "NilsSve_DUFLibrary26.0-25ae4a4d", but "NilsSve_DUFLibrary26.0"
       must never be claimed by a folder called "lib". */
    Function PackageFolderFor String sHome String sLibFolder Returns String
        tRFSearchResult[] aDirs
        String  sKey sCand
        Integer i iLast

        Move (NormalisedFolderName(Self, sLibFolder)) to sKey
        If (sKey = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (rfFileSearch((vFolderFormat(sHome) + "DfPkg" + CS_DirSeparator + "*.*"), DIRMODE_DIRECTORIES_ONLY, False)) to aDirs
        Move (SizeOfArray(aDirs) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Trim(aDirs[i].sFilename)) to sCand
            If (sCand <> "" and sCand <> "." and sCand <> "..") Begin
                If ((NormalisedFolderName(Self, sCand)) contains sKey) ;
                    Function_Return (vFolderFormat(sHome) + "DfPkg" + CS_DirSeparator + sCand)
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    /* PURE. True for the extensions WorkspaceSourceFiles sweeps - see SourceLeafExtensions.
       Declared ABOVE its caller deliberately: it is read from an EXPRESSION, and DataFlex resolves
       those at the point of use, not at the end of the class. */
    Function IsSourceLeaf String sLeaf Returns Boolean
        String[] asExt
        Integer i iLast

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sLeaf))) to sLeaf
        Get SourceLeafExtensions to asExt
        Move (SizeOfArray(asExt) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Right(sLeaf, Length(asExt[i])) = asExt[i]) ;
                Function_Return True
        Loop
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    /* How a stale library folder compares with the package that replaced it. Fills the three counts
       the reader actually needs to judge a cleanup:
         iOnlyHere - source files present in the folder and in NO form in the package. THE decisive
                     number: it is what would be lost, and on one real workspace it was 86 of 154
                     (an old DUF tree carrying its own sub-libraries, which are separate packages now).
         iDiffer   - same file name, different SIZE. Compared by size, not content: enough to say
                     "these are not the same file", cheap enough to run over a whole tree.
         iSame     - same name, same size.
       Counting SOURCE files only (the WorkspaceSourceFiles extensions), because a stray .bak or an
       image says nothing about whether code would be lost. */
    Procedure FolderVersusPackage String sLibDir String sPkgDir Integer ByRef iSame Integer ByRef iDiffer Integer ByRef iOnlyHere
        tRFSearchResult[] aLib aPkg
        String[] asPkgLeaf
        Integer[] aiPkgSize
        String  sLeaf
        Integer i iLast iAt

        Move 0 to iSame
        Move 0 to iDiffer
        Move 0 to iOnlyHere
        Move (rfFileSearchRecursive((vFolderFormat(sPkgDir) + "*.*"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aPkg
        Move (SizeOfArray(aPkg) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(ExtractFileName(aPkg[i].sFilename))) to sLeaf
            Move sLeaf to asPkgLeaf[SizeOfArray(asPkgLeaf)]
            Move (rfFileSize(aPkg[i].sFilename)) to aiPkgSize[SizeOfArray(aiPkgSize)]
        Loop
        Move (rfFileSearchRecursive((vFolderFormat(sLibDir) + "*.*"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aLib
        Move (SizeOfArray(aLib) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(ExtractFileName(aLib[i].sFilename))) to sLeaf
            If (IsSourceLeaf(Self, sLeaf) = True) Begin
                Move (SearchArray(sLeaf, asPkgLeaf)) to iAt
                If (iAt = -1) ;
                    Increment iOnlyHere
                Else If (aiPkgSize[iAt] = (rfFileSize(aLib[i].sFilename))) ;
                    Increment iSame
                Else ;
                    Increment iDiffer
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    /* PURE. The library FOLDER a removed .sws entry belongs to, or "" when there is nothing this
       tool may touch. Given the workspace home and an entry as the .sws records it - relative or
       absolute - it answers the DIRECT CHILD of <home>\Libraries that contains it.

       Walking up to that child rather than taking the .sws file's own parent, because a library
       routinely keeps its .sws in a subfolder: vWin32fh's lives in StudioLibrary\, so the parent is
       Libraries\vwin32fh\StudioLibrary and retiring THAT would leave the library half-present and
       still findable.

       Answers "" for an entry that does not live under <home>\Libraries at all. A library declared
       by absolute path into another project is shared with whatever else declares it, and a folder
       outside the workspace is not this workspace's to rename - the one case where doing nothing is
       obviously right. */
    Function RetirableLibraryFolder String sHome String sEntry Returns String
        String sPath sRoot sLow sRootLow sRest sName
        Integer iAt

        Move (Trim(sEntry)) to sPath
        If (sPath = "" or Trim(sHome) = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Replaces("/", sPath, CS_DirSeparator)) to sPath
        // Relative entries are written relative to the workspace home (RelativeLibraryEntry).
        If (not(sPath contains ":")) ;
            Move (vFolderFormat(sHome) + sPath) to sPath
        Move (vFolderFormat(sHome) + "Libraries" + CS_DirSeparator) to sRoot
        Move (Lowercase(sPath)) to sLow
        Move (Lowercase(sRoot)) to sRootLow
        If (Left(sLow, Length(sRootLow)) <> sRootLow) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Right(sPath, (Length(sPath) - Length(sRoot)))) to sRest
        Move (Pos(CS_DirSeparator, sRest)) to iAt
        If (iAt < 2) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Left(sRest, (iAt - 1))) to sName
        Function_Return (sRoot + sName)
    End_Function

    /* PURE. The direct children of <home>\Libraries that asBefore's entries point into and asNow's
       do not - what a change to the library list stopped using - each once, in asBefore's order.

       FOLDER AGAINST FOLDER, never entry against entry (2026-09-11). One folder can hold more than
       one .sws - a library ships one per release, which is how these are versioned - so dropping one
       entry does not orphan a folder a sibling entry still names. And the SAME entry is written
       differently once df-cli has converted the file - "Libraries\X\X.sws" in [Libraries],
       "Libraries/X/X.sws" in a JSON dependency - which an entry compare would read as a removal. A
       git dependency names no folder at all, so the library it replaced drops out, which is the
       point. Whether the folder is still ON DISK, and whether something further down the chain
       still declares it, are the caller's questions (vFolderExists, IsOrphanedLibraryFolder). */
    Function LibraryFoldersNoLongerListed String sHome String[] asBefore String[] asNow Returns String[]
        String[] asNowLow asSeenLow asOut
        String sFolder sLow
        Integer i iMax

        Move (SizeOfArray(asNow) - 1) to iMax
        For i from 0 to iMax
            Get RetirableLibraryFolder sHome asNow[i] to sFolder
            If (sFolder <> "") ;
                Move (Lowercase(sFolder)) to asNowLow[SizeOfArray(asNowLow)]
        Loop
        Move (SizeOfArray(asBefore) - 1) to iMax
        For i from 0 to iMax
            Get RetirableLibraryFolder sHome asBefore[i] to sFolder
            Move (Lowercase(sFolder)) to sLow
            If (sFolder <> "" and SearchArray(sLow, asNowLow) = -1 and SearchArray(sLow, asSeenLow) = -1) Begin
                Move sLow    to asSeenLow[SizeOfArray(asSeenLow)]
                Move sFolder to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    /* ---- THE LIBRARY FOLDER A PACKAGE REPLACED -------------------------------------------

       Nils 2026-09-10: "If libraries were also ticked when a workspace was copied to a new
       location, and then they were removed from the Libraries dialog + packages added in their
       place ... the analyzer searches both the libraries and packages, aka there are duplicates."

       IT IS NOT DUPLICATES, and that is worse. A DfPkg checkout is excluded from the refactoring
       scope (CS_NoFolderList, since 2026-08-18) and a folder under <home>\Libraries is not - it is
       an ordinary folder under the home, found by the ordinary home scan. So the two are never
       BOTH scanned: the one the compiler builds is out of scope, and the one it abandoned is in.
       The user then fixes a warning in a file that takes no part in the build, rebuilds, and the
       warning is still there - the failure this whole class exists to name.

       AND NOTHING ALREADY HERE DROPS IT. RemoveLibraryFolders (the "Include library folders"
       untick) deletes only rows that are under a declared library root AND NOT under the home, so
       a library inside <home>\Libraries fails the second test; and once the .sws stops declaring
       it, it is not a library root any more either. RemoveSystemFolders takes only CS_NoFolderList
       names. MaintainLibrariesFT asks when its dialog closes after a showing that stopped using a
       folder (OfferRetireAfterClose, 2026-09-11 - an offer at OK before that) - event-driven, so a
       workspace copied while already in this state, or one where the question was declined, is
       not asked again. This is the standing detector for that state. */

    /* PURE. Is this direct child of <home>\Libraries one that nothing declares any more?

       THE DECLARATION TEST IS BY PATH, NOT BY NAME. A "does any .sws mention it" test - which
       SwsDeclarationText below answers, for a different question - reads FALSE here: a git
       dependency names the library in its URL precisely BECAUSE it is now a package
       ("https://github.com/Someone/Library-DUF.git" contains "duf"), so the folder it replaced
       would look declared for ever. asDeclaredLibPaths is the caller's list of library SOURCE
       folders actually declared by the workspace - GetWorkspaceLibrarySourceFolders, which follows
       local dependencies and skips git ones - and a folder is declared when any of them is AT or
       UNDER it.

       A folder an earlier round already retired is not offered again: <name>.OLD, and .OLD2 upward
       when the first name was taken. Only the last segment is judged, so a workspace living under
       a path with ".old" in it is unaffected. */
    Function IsOrphanedLibraryFolder String sLibFolder String[] asDeclaredLibPaths Returns Boolean
        String  sLow sName sDecl
        Integer i iMax iAt

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sLibFolder))) to sLow
        If (sLow = "") ;
            Function_Return False
        If (Right(sLow, 1) = CS_DirSeparator) ;
            Move (Left(sLow, (Length(sLow) - 1))) to sLow
        Move (RightPos(CS_DirSeparator, sLow)) to iAt
        If (iAt > 0) ;
            Move (Right(sLow, (Length(sLow) - iAt))) to sName
        Else ;
            Move sLow to sName
        If (sName contains ".old") ;
            Function_Return False
        Move (SizeOfArray(asDeclaredLibPaths) - 1) to iMax
        For i from 0 to iMax
            Move (Lowercase(Trim(asDeclaredLibPaths[i]))) to sDecl
            If (Right(sDecl, 1) = CS_DirSeparator) ;
                Move (Left(sDecl, (Length(sDecl) - 1))) to sDecl
            If (sDecl <> "") Begin
                If (sDecl = sLow) ;
                    Function_Return False
                If (Left(sDecl, (Length(sLow) + 1)) = (sLow + CS_DirSeparator)) ;
                    Function_Return False
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    /* PURE. The name a retire should give sFolder, given the sibling names already TAKEN
       (lowercased, full paths): <name>.OLD, or the first free <name>.OLD2, .OLD3 ... and "" when
       even .OLD99 is taken - which the caller reports rather than guessing further.

       Pure so the numbering is testable: it is the one part of a retire that can quietly destroy
       the copy a previous retire left behind, and rfRenameFile REFUSES to overwrite, so a wrong
       name here shows up as a failure rather than a loss - but only if the numbering is right. */
    Function RetireTargetName String sFolder String[] asTakenLower Returns String
        String  sBase sTry
        Integer iN

        Move (Trim(sFolder)) to sBase
        If (sBase = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        If (Right(sBase, 1) = CS_DirSeparator) ;
            Move (Left(sBase, (Length(sBase) - 1))) to sBase
        Move (sBase + ".OLD") to sTry
        Move 2 to iN
        While (SearchArray(Lowercase(sTry), asTakenLower) <> -1 and iN < 100)
            Move (sBase + ".OLD" + String(iN)) to sTry
            Increment iN
        Loop
        If (SearchArray(Lowercase(sTry), asTakenLower) <> -1) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return sTry
    End_Function

    /* PURE - the FILE twin of RetireTargetName (Nils 2026-09-14). The name a retire gives a shadowing
       COPY, given the sibling names already taken (lowercased, full paths): <file>.shadowed, or the
       first free <file>.shadowed2, .shadowed3 ... and "" when even .shadowed99 is taken.

       Why a number is needed at all: a first [Rename them] leaves <file>.shadowed, a Revert moves the
       backup back as the live file, "Offer them again" forgets the retire, and the next [Rename them]
       asked rfRenameFile to move the file onto its own twin - refused, as it must be (that twin is a
       copy only a hand can restore from), and reported as "a file of that name already exists" three
       times over on a real copy, while the row kept offering the same press. A taken twin is not a
       failure; it is a number. Nothing is deleted either way. */
    Function ShadowTargetName String sFile String[] asTakenLower Returns String
        String  sBase sTry
        Integer iN

        Move (Trim(sFile)) to sBase
        If (sBase = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (sBase + ".shadowed") to sTry
        Move 2 to iN
        While (SearchArray(Lowercase(sTry), asTakenLower) <> -1 and iN < 100)
            Move (sBase + ".shadowed" + String(iN)) to sTry
            Increment iN
        Loop
        If (SearchArray(Lowercase(sTry), asTakenLower) <> -1) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return sTry
    End_Function

    // The <file>.shadowed* siblings already on disk beside sFile, lowercased full paths - what
    // ShadowTargetName must step past.
    Function _ShadowNamesTaken String sFile Returns String[]
        tRFSearchResult[] aFound
        String[] asOut
        String  sFolder sLeaf
        Integer i iPos

        Move (RightPos(CS_DirSeparator, sFile)) to iPos
        If (iPos = 0) ;
            Function_Return asOut
        Move (Left(sFile, iPos)) to sFolder
        Move (Right(sFile, (Length(sFile) - iPos))) to sLeaf
        Move (rfFileSearch((sFolder + sLeaf + ".shadowed*"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFound
        For i from 0 to (SizeOfArray(aFound) - 1)
            Move (Lowercase(sFolder + aFound[i].sFilename)) to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // Are two files the same content? Size first, then the lines - a source file, read whole.
    Function _SameFileContent String sA String sB Returns Boolean
        String[] asA asB

        If (rfFileSizeLive(sA) <> rfFileSizeLive(sB)) ;
            Function_Return False
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sA)) to asA
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sB)) to asB
        Function_Return (IsSameArray(asA, asB))
    End_Function

    /* Renames one library folder out of the compiler's reach, filling sNewName and returning ""
       on success or the reason it failed. RENAMED, NEVER DELETED, for the reason
       MaintainLibrariesFT._RetireLibraryFolders gives: these trees are not copies of the package
       that replaced them - one real Libraries\DUF held 86 source files present in no form in its
       package - and the undo for a rename is renaming back. */
    Function RetireLibraryFolder String sFolder String ByRef sNewName Returns String
        tRFSearchResult[] aDirs
        String[] asTaken
        String  sParent sTarget sCand
        Integer i iLast iAt

        Move "" to sNewName
        Move (Trim(sFolder)) to sFolder
        If (sFolder = "") ;
            Function_Return "no folder given"
        If (Right(sFolder, 1) = CS_DirSeparator) ;
            Move (Left(sFolder, (Length(sFolder) - 1))) to sFolder
        If (rfDirectoryExists(sFolder) = False) ;
            Function_Return ("the folder is no longer there: " + sFolder)
        Move (RightPos(CS_DirSeparator, sFolder)) to iAt
        If (iAt < 2) ;
            Function_Return ("not a folder this may rename: " + sFolder)
        Move (Left(sFolder, (iAt - 1))) to sParent
        // Every sibling, so the numbering below steps over a name an earlier retire already owns.
        Move (rfFileSearch((vFolderFormat(sParent) + "*.*"), DIRMODE_DIRECTORIES_ONLY, False)) to aDirs
        Move (SizeOfArray(aDirs) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Trim(aDirs[i].sFilename)) to sCand
            If (sCand <> "" and sCand <> "." and sCand <> "..") ;
                Move (Lowercase(vFolderFormat(sParent) + sCand)) to asTaken[SizeOfArray(asTaken)]
        Loop
        Get RetireTargetName sFolder asTaken to sTarget
        If (sTarget = "") ;
            Function_Return ("every .OLD name up to 99 is already taken beside: " + sFolder)
        Move sTarget to sNewName
        Function_Return (rfRenameFile(sFolder, sTarget))
    End_Function

    /* Every direct child of <home>\Libraries that a PACKAGE has replaced and nothing declares:
       fills the folder, its package, and the three counts FolderVersusPackage takes, and returns
       how many. The counts are what makes the offer judgeable rather than a bare warning -
       ONLY-HERE above all, because that is what a rename would put out of reach.

       A folder holding no source at all is skipped: an empty shell left by a copy cannot shadow
       anything, and offering to rename it is noise. The package match is PackageFolderFor's, which
       is by normalised name - the same test the report has used since 2026-08-30. */
    Function OrphanedLibraryFolders String sHome String[] asDeclaredLibPaths ;
            String[] ByRef asFolder String[] ByRef asPkg Integer[] ByRef aiSame ;
            Integer[] ByRef aiDiffer Integer[] ByRef aiOnlyHere Returns Integer
        tRFSearchResult[] aDirs
        String  sLibRoot sChild sLib sPkg
        Integer i iLast iSame iDiffer iOnlyHere

        Move (Trim(sHome)) to sHome
        If (sHome = "") ;
            Function_Return 0
        Move (vFolderFormat(sHome) + "Libraries") to sLibRoot
        If (rfDirectoryExists(sLibRoot) = False) ;
            Function_Return 0
        Move (rfFileSearch((vFolderFormat(sLibRoot) + "*.*"), DIRMODE_DIRECTORIES_ONLY, False)) to aDirs
        Move (SizeOfArray(aDirs) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Trim(aDirs[i].sFilename)) to sChild
            If (sChild <> "" and sChild <> "." and sChild <> "..") Begin
                Move (vFolderFormat(sLibRoot) + sChild) to sLib
                If (IsOrphanedLibraryFolder(Self, sLib, asDeclaredLibPaths) = True) Begin
                    Get PackageFolderFor sHome sChild to sPkg
                    If (sPkg <> "") Begin
                        Send FolderVersusPackage sLib sPkg (&iSame) (&iDiffer) (&iOnlyHere)
                        If ((iSame + iDiffer + iOnlyHere) > 0) Begin
                            Move sLib      to asFolder[SizeOfArray(asFolder)]
                            Move sPkg      to asPkg[SizeOfArray(asPkg)]
                            Move iSame     to aiSame[SizeOfArray(aiSame)]
                            Move iDiffer   to aiDiffer[SizeOfArray(aiDiffer)]
                            Move iOnlyHere to aiOnlyHere[SizeOfArray(aiOnlyHere)]
                        End
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return (SizeOfArray(asFolder))
    End_Function

    /* Every .sws in the workspace home, as ONE lowercased blob - the cheapest honest test of "is
       this folder still declared". A folder is only reported when the listing shows nothing of it
       was compiled AND no .sws so much as mentions its name, so a library used by a DIFFERENT
       project in the same workspace is never called stale on one program's evidence. */
    Function SwsDeclarationText String sHome Returns String
        tRFSearchResult[] aFound
        String[] asLines
        String  sBlob
        Integer i iLast j jLast

        Move (rfFileSearch((vFolderFormat(sHome) + "*.sws"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFound
        Move (SizeOfArray(aFound) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(vFolderFormat(sHome) + aFound[i].sFilename)) to asLines
            Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to jLast
            For j from 0 to jLast
                Move (sBlob + " " + Lowercase(asLines[j])) to sBlob
            Loop
        Loop
        Function_Return sBlob
    End_Function

    /* PURE. Is this path the WORKSPACE OWN source, rather than a package pool or a library folder?

       This is the whole discriminator for PART 3, and it was measured before it was written. Every
       workspace shares some file names with the DataFlex install - 10 on one legacy workspace, 28 on
       another - so "you have a file called like an install file" is noise. Splitting them by WHERE
       the winning copy lives separates the two populations exactly:

         DfPkg\ or Libraries\  a package or library that legitimately carries that name. Nils own
                               DfAbout.pkg, StdAbout.pkg, cSelectFolderDialog.pkg and MSSqldrv.pkg
                               all shadow install files ON PURPOSE - four of them on one workspace,
                               and not one is a defect.
         anywhere else         the applications OWN copy of a vendor file, which is the dangerous
                               kind: it is usually decades old, and it wins.

       Judged on the path only. Reading the file could not answer it - a deliberate fork and a stale
       leftover look identical inside. */
    Function IsWorkspaceOwnSource String sPath String sHome Returns Boolean
        String sLow sHomeLow

        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sPath))) to sLow
        Move (Lowercase(vFolderFormat(Trim(sHome)))) to sHomeLow
        If (sLow = "" or sHomeLow = "") ;
            Function_Return False
        If (Left(sLow, Length(sHomeLow)) <> sHomeLow) ;
            Function_Return False
        If (Pos((CS_DirSeparator + "dfpkg" + CS_DirSeparator), sLow) > 0) ;
            Function_Return False
        If (Pos((CS_DirSeparator + "libraries" + CS_DirSeparator), sLow) > 0) ;
            Function_Return False
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    /* PURE. A file a library ships as a TEMPLATE for the application to generate and keep - a
       same-named copy that is right by design, and it must never be offered a rename.
       LoginEncryptionKey.inc is the Studio's per-application encryption key (Nils 2026-09-15:
       "always leave LoginEncryptionKey.inc, it is a Studio auto-generated encryption file"); DUF,
       VDFQuery and the Filesystem library each ship one, so it turned up in four of the five
       workspaces measured, DIFFERENT from the pool's every time. Excluded here, in the one place
       every reference set passes through (CopiesAgainstReference). */
    Function IsPerAppGeneratedFile String sLeaf Returns Boolean
        Function_Return (Lowercase(Trim(sLeaf)) = "loginencryptionkey.inc")
    End_Function

    /* PURE, and the exact MIRROR of IsPerAppGeneratedFile above: a named file that must always be
       SUGGESTED for rename, even though its bytes differ from the shipped one (Nils 2026-09-16:
       "errornum.inc should always have a suggestion to be renamed").

       The tick means "renaming this loses nothing". bSame is one way to know that; this list is the
       other. errornum.inc earns its place because it does not merely differ - it STARVES the file it
       stands in front of. The 1992 copy measured on a real workspace holds 300 #REPLACEs whose values
       are all identical to the install's, ZERO constants of its own, and is MISSING 93; its
       "#IFDEF ERRORNUM_INCLUDED" guard then takes the install copy's include guard, so the real file
       never loads and every one of those 93 comes back undefined - the 573-error cascade that read
       like an application bug for days. There is nothing in it to preserve, so the general
       "DIFFERENT => let a human look" default is wrong here in the same way it was wrong for
       LoginEncryptionKey.inc in the other direction.

       Suggested, never forced: the row is only TICKED, and the user can untick it like any other. */
    Function IsAlwaysRetireFile String sLeaf Returns Boolean
        Function_Return (Lowercase(Trim(sLeaf)) = "errornum.inc")
    End_Function

    /* THE ONE SYSTEM FILE A WORKSPACE HOLDS ON PURPOSE: ITS LANGUAGE (Nils 2026-11-05).

       Language_Current.inc names the language DataFlex's own texts compile in, and includes that
       language's texts. The docs (Selecting Your Language) place it in DataFlex\Pkg, where the
       installer sets it; Usr\Language\<language>\Pkg ships one per language. They never mention a
       copy in a workspace, but one does the same job for that one workspace, because its folder is
       searched first. So it is a setting, not an outdated copy, and renaming it has nothing to gain.

       MEASURED on scratch compiles with a Swedish workspace's own files:

         the file and its text files          0 errors, the exe says Avbryt, never Cancel
         renamed away                         0 errors, the exe says Cancel, never Avbryt
         the file, its text files not found   238 errors, no exe
         only the Define, no #Include         237 errors, no exe

       The second row is what [Rename them] did to a real workspace, behind a dialog that only said
       DIFFERENT. So a file that names its language AND includes its texts gets no row at all
       (_SetsALanguage, in the one place the rows are made, because the answer needs the file's
       lines). The fourth row is the exception: LanguageText.pkg used to include the texts itself,
       and a copy from then now leaves every C_$ text undefined. That one is broken, and stays listed.

       THE TEXT FILES KEEP THE GENERAL RULE. Language_<language>.inc and its DD, WebApp and WinPrint
       files get a row only when the install ships the same name, so a rename still finds the shipped
       text and the language stays. */
    Function IsLanguageSettingLeaf String sLeaf Returns Boolean
        Function_Return (Lowercase(Trim(sLeaf)) = Lowercase(CS_LanguageSettingFile))
    End_Function

    /* PURE. The language these lines of a Language_Current.inc pick ("Svenska"), with the file they
       include, or "" when they do not both name a language and include its texts. Only what stands
       before a // counts. */
    Function LanguageSettingOf String[] ByRef asLines String ByRef sInclude Returns String
        String sLine sLow sLanguage sName
        Integer i iLast iAt

        Move "" to sLanguage
        Move "" to sInclude
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Replaces(Character(9), asLines[i], " ")) to sLine
            Move (Pos("//", sLine)) to iAt
            If (iAt > 0) ;
                Move (Left(sLine, (iAt - 1))) to sLine
            Move (Trim(sLine)) to sLine
            Move (Lowercase(sLine)) to sLow
            If (Pos("#include ", sLow) = 1) ;
                Move (Trim(Right(sLine, (Length(sLine) - 9)))) to sInclude
            If (Pos("define ", sLow) = 1 and Pos(" language$current ", sLow) > 0) Begin
                Move (Pos(" for ", sLow)) to iAt
                If (iAt > 0) Begin
                    Move (Trim(Right(sLine, (Length(sLine) - iAt - 4)))) to sName
                    If (Pos("language$", Lowercase(sName)) = 1) ;
                        Move (Right(sName, (Length(sName) - 9))) to sLanguage
                End
            End
        Loop
        If (sInclude = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return sLanguage
    End_Function

    // Does this copy set a language? Reads the file only for the one name that can.
    Function _SetsALanguage String sLeaf String sPath Returns Boolean
        String[] asLines
        String sInclude sLanguage

        If (IsLanguageSettingLeaf(Self, sLeaf) = False) ;
            Function_Return False
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sPath)) to asLines
        Get LanguageSettingOf (&asLines) (&sInclude) to sLanguage
        Function_Return (sLanguage <> "")
    End_Function

    /* PURE. Every copy in the workspace's OWN source of a file a reference set ships, classified by
       whether THIS build read it. A classifier against ANY reference set: the install's shipped
       names (InstallCopiesClassified) are the only one asked since 2026-10-05; from 2026-09-15 until
       then the names the workspace's libraries ship were a second. Two classes, one list:

         class 0 - the listing names the workspace copy as the compiled one: it OVERRIDES the
                   shipped file. The 2026-08-30 finding, unchanged.
         class 1 - the workspace carries the file under a shipped name and the build did NOT
                   read it: its folder is off the search path, or nothing Uses it. It compiles
                   nothing today and wins the day the compiler reaches it. A 1997 copy of a
                   treeview package sat in a side folder of a workspace for years exactly so -
                   nine views Use the name, the installed copy compiled, and nothing said the
                   old one was there, one path edit away from winning (Nils 2026-09-13: "I would
                   like to also have system file copies that are not reached by the compiler
                   offered a rename"). Renaming one changes nothing THIS build compiled -
                   a program the listing does not cover may still reach it on its own build,
                   which is why the dialog says so rather than calling the rename free.

       asLeaf / asWinner are the listing's compiled names (lowercased) and paths; asAll is the
       sweep of every source file under the home; asRefLower / asRefPath the reference names,
       lowercased, and the path shipping each (parallel). No file system access - the caller
       supplies all of it, which is what makes this testable. Fills four parallel arrays and
       returns the count; the compiled copy is never listed a second time from the sweep, and a
       per-application generated file (IsPerAppGeneratedFile) is never listed at all. */
    Function CopiesAgainstReference String[] ByRef asLeaf String[] ByRef asWinner String[] ByRef asAll ;
            String[] ByRef asRefLower String[] ByRef asRefPath String sHome ;
            String[] ByRef asOutLeaf String[] ByRef asOutPath String[] ByRef asOutShipped Integer[] ByRef aiClass Returns Integer
        String[] asWinLower
        String sLow sLeafLow sLeaf
        Integer i iLast iCount iRef
        Boolean bOwn

        Move (ResizeArray(asOutLeaf, 0))    to asOutLeaf
        Move (ResizeArray(asOutPath, 0))    to asOutPath
        Move (ResizeArray(asOutShipped, 0)) to asOutShipped
        Move (ResizeArray(aiClass, 0))      to aiClass
        Move 0 to iCount
        // class 0 - the compiled copy is the workspace's own
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLeaf) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(Trim(asWinner[i]))) to sLow
            Move sLow to asWinLower[SizeOfArray(asWinLower)]
            Get IsWorkspaceOwnSource asWinner[i] sHome to bOwn
            If (bOwn = True) Begin
                Move (Lowercase(Trim(asLeaf[i]))) to sLeafLow
                Move (SearchArray(sLeafLow, asRefLower)) to iRef
                If (iRef <> -1 and IsPerAppGeneratedFile(Self, sLeafLow) = False) Begin
                    Move asLeaf[i]      to asOutLeaf[iCount]
                    Move asWinner[i]    to asOutPath[iCount]
                    Move asRefPath[iRef] to asOutShipped[iCount]
                    Move 0 to aiClass[iCount]
                    Increment iCount
                End
            End
        Loop
        // class 1 - carried under a shipped name, and not what this build compiled
        Move (SizeOfArray(asAll) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(Trim(asAll[i]))) to sLow
            If (sLow <> "") Begin
                If (SearchArray(sLow, asWinLower) = -1) Begin
                    Move (FileLeafLower(sLow)) to sLeafLow
                    Move (SearchArray(sLeafLow, asRefLower)) to iRef
                    If (iRef <> -1 and IsPerAppGeneratedFile(Self, sLeafLow) = False) Begin
                        Get IsWorkspaceOwnSource asAll[i] sHome to bOwn
                        If (bOwn = True) Begin
                            Move (ExtractFileName(Trim(asAll[i]))) to sLeaf
                            Move sLeaf            to asOutLeaf[iCount]
                            Move (Trim(asAll[i])) to asOutPath[iCount]
                            Move asRefPath[iRef]  to asOutShipped[iCount]
                            Move 1 to aiClass[iCount]
                            Increment iCount
                        End
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return iCount
    End_Function

    /* PURE. The file an ERROR line of a listing names - "ERROR: 52 ... ON LINE: 67 (67) OF FILE:
       E:\Ws\DfPkg\...\dates.nui" - or "" for any other line, a warning included. */
    Function ErrorFileFromPrnLine String sLine Returns String
        String sTrim
        Integer iAt

        Move (Trim(sLine)) to sTrim
        If (Uppercase(Left(sTrim, 6)) <> "ERROR:") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Pos("OF FILE:", Uppercase(sTrim))) to iAt
        If (iAt = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (Trim(Right(sTrim, (Length(sTrim) - iAt - 7))))
    End_Function

    /* PURE. THE SECOND KIND OF ROW (2026-11-12): a copy in the workspace's OWN source that this build
       compiled in place of a file a package checkout ships, where that package has ERRORS in the same
       build.

       Nils's rule of 2026-10-05 stands - a file name a library also uses is no finding - and this is
       its one exception, proposed on 2026-11-05 and taken up on 2026-11-12. Measured on a real
       workspace: its AppSrc held a LANGUAGE.PKG from before the library was a package, the search
       path reached it first, and VDFQuery20's dates.nui compiled against it - 76 errors, every one in
       a package file nobody can edit, the board saying "fix it where the package is maintained", and
       nothing naming the copy. With the library's own language.pkg in its place: the 76 gone, 0 new.

       THE TRIGGER IS NARROW. Only a copy the listing names as COMPILED (a copy the build did not read
       cannot cause this build's errors), only in front of a file in DfPkg or the package cache, and
       only when that package's files carry errors in the same listing. That is a correlation, not a
       proof - the package may fail for reasons of its own - so the row is ticked only when the two
       files are identical, as every other row, and the board says "may".

       asLeaf / asWinner are the listing's compiled names and paths, asAll the sweep of the home and
       asErrFiles the files the listing's ERROR lines name (ErrorFileFromPrnLine), one per error.
       Fills four parallel arrays - the copy's leaf and path, the package's file of that name, and the
       package's error count - and returns the count. */
    Function FailingPackageCopies String[] ByRef asLeaf String[] ByRef asWinner String[] ByRef asAll ;
            String[] ByRef asErrFiles String sHome ;
            String[] ByRef asOutLeaf String[] ByRef asOutPath String[] ByRef asOutShipped Integer[] ByRef aiErrors Returns Integer
        String[] asRoot asPoolLeaf asPoolPath
        Integer[] aiRootErr aiPoolErr
        String sRoot sLeafLow
        Integer i iLast iAt iCount
        Boolean bOwn

        Move (ResizeArray(asOutLeaf, 0))    to asOutLeaf
        Move (ResizeArray(asOutPath, 0))    to asOutPath
        Move (ResizeArray(asOutShipped, 0)) to asOutShipped
        Move (ResizeArray(aiErrors, 0))     to aiErrors
        // the packages with errors in this build, and how many each has
        Move (SizeOfArray(asErrFiles) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(PoolPackageRootOf(asErrFiles[i]))) to sRoot
            If (sRoot <> "") Begin
                Move (SearchArray(sRoot, asRoot)) to iAt
                If (iAt = -1) Begin
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asRoot)) to iAt
                    Move sRoot to asRoot[iAt]
                    Move 0     to aiRootErr[iAt]
                End
                Move (aiRootErr[iAt] + 1) to aiRootErr[iAt]
            End
        Loop
        If (SizeOfArray(asRoot) = 0) ;
            Function_Return 0
        // every file those packages ship, by name - one pass over the sweep
        Move (SizeOfArray(asAll) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Lowercase(PoolPackageRootOf(asAll[i]))) to sRoot
            If (sRoot <> "") Begin
                Move (SearchArray(sRoot, asRoot)) to iAt
                If (iAt <> -1) Begin
                    Move (FileLeafLower(asAll[i])) to asPoolLeaf[SizeOfArray(asPoolLeaf)]
                    Move (Trim(asAll[i]))          to asPoolPath[SizeOfArray(asPoolPath)]
                    Move aiRootErr[iAt]            to aiPoolErr[SizeOfArray(aiPoolErr)]
                End
            End
        Loop
        // the workspace's own copies this build compiled under one of those names
        Move 0 to iCount
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLeaf) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Get IsWorkspaceOwnSource asWinner[i] sHome to bOwn
            If (bOwn = True) Begin
                Move (Lowercase(Trim(asLeaf[i]))) to sLeafLow
                Move (SearchArray(sLeafLow, asPoolLeaf)) to iAt
                If (iAt <> -1 and IsPerAppGeneratedFile(Self, sLeafLow) = False) Begin
                    Move (ExtractFileName(Trim(asWinner[i]))) to asOutLeaf[iCount]
                    Move (Trim(asWinner[i])) to asOutPath[iCount]
                    Move asPoolPath[iAt]     to asOutShipped[iCount]
                    Move aiPoolErr[iAt]      to aiErrors[iCount]
                    Increment iCount
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return iCount
    End_Function

    /* PURE. One row from one classified copy. bSame / bTicked are left False: they need the two
       files' bytes, which the caller with file access fills in (_AppendShadowRows). */
    Function ShadowRowFrom String sLeaf String sPath String sShipped Integer eKind Integer iClass Returns tShadowCopy
        tShadowCopy Row

        Move (Trim(sLeaf))    to Row.sLeaf
        Move (Trim(sPath))    to Row.sPath
        Move (Trim(sShipped)) to Row.sShipped
        Move eKind  to Row.eKind
        Move iClass to Row.iClass
        Move "DataFlex" to Row.sSource
        Move False to Row.bSame
        Move False to Row.bTicked
        Function_Return Row
    End_Function

    // The install's shipped file names (SourceLeafExtensions), lowercased - the reference set a
    // workspace copy of a system file is judged against. rfFileSearch answers bare names, which is
    // exactly the spelling the compare wants.
    Function InstallShippedNames String sInstall Returns String[]
        tRFSearchResult[] aFound
        String[] asExt asOut
        Integer iMask iMaskLast iFile iLast

        If (Trim(sInstall) = "") ;
            Function_Return asOut
        Get SourceLeafExtensions to asExt
        Move (SizeOfArray(asExt) - 1) to iMaskLast
        For iMask from 0 to iMaskLast
            Move (rfFileSearch((vFolderFormat(sInstall) + "*" + asExt[iMask]), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFound
            Move (SizeOfArray(aFound) - 1) to iLast
            For iFile from 0 to iLast
                If (Trim(aFound[iFile].sFilename) <> "") ;
                    Move (Lowercase(Trim(aFound[iFile].sFilename))) to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
            Loop
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    /* PURE. Every copy of a DataFlex system file in the workspace's OWN source, classified by
       whether THIS build read it - CopiesAgainstReference over the install's shipped names, each
       standing for <install>\<name>. The shipped path is spelled with the copy's own leaf, as the
       install folder spells it on disk. Kept as the install kind's entry (and its tests' seam)
       when the pool kind arrived on 2026-09-15. */
    Function InstallCopiesClassified String[] ByRef asLeaf String[] ByRef asWinner String[] ByRef asAll ;
            String[] ByRef asShippedLower String sHome String sInstall ;
            String[] ByRef asOutLeaf String[] ByRef asOutPath String[] ByRef asOutInst Integer[] ByRef aiClass Returns Integer
        String[] asRefPath
        Integer i iLast iCount

        Move (SizeOfArray(asShippedLower) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (vFolderFormat(sInstall) + asShippedLower[i]) to asRefPath[i]
        Loop
        Get CopiesAgainstReference (&asLeaf) (&asWinner) (&asAll) (&asShippedLower) (&asRefPath) sHome ;
            (&asOutLeaf) (&asOutPath) (&asOutInst) (&aiClass) to iCount
        Move (iCount - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (vFolderFormat(sInstall) + asOutLeaf[i]) to asOutInst[i]
        Loop
        Function_Return iCount
    End_Function


    /* PART 3 - the workspace overriding a file of DataFlex OWN, which is the most serious shape this
       report can find and the one it was blind to until 2026-08-30 - and PART 4, its commoner
       cousin since 2026-09-15: the workspace's own copy of a file one of its LIBRARIES ships.

       WHAT PART 3 COSTS, from the workspace that prompted it: a legacy application carried its own
       errornum.inc - the file that defines every DFERR_* constant - dated 1992 and holding 299 of the
       392 the installed DataFlex defines. Its folder is on the appSrc path, so it WON; and because it
       opens with #IFDEF ERRORNUM_INCLUDED it also claimed the include guard, so the real one could
       never load afterwards. DataFlex own packages then failed to compile against DataFlex own
       constants: 573 errors, every one of them pointing at an innocent install file, and the last of
       them a 4391 that read like a broken Object in the users source. Nothing in the workspace looked
       wrong, and the file had not been touched in decades.

       WHAT PART 4 COSTS (Nils 2026-09-15, on a migration copy: "one or several files from an
       external library were copied to the workspace AppSrc folder. This can of course create lots
       of problems and worse, those problems can be hard to track down"). Measured across five
       workspaces: one to five such copies each, and EVERY one differed from the library's file -
       old versions of the library's own packages, compiled in its place. So the same rename is
       offered, file by file, with the content compared: an identical copy loses nothing, a
       different one is a fork until someone looks.

       WHY THE EXISTING PARTS COULD NOT SEE EITHER: parts 1 and 2 compare workspace copies with EACH
       OTHER. A system-file copy exists exactly once under the home, so it is not a duplicate by any
       measure they take; a library-file copy IS a duplicate, but so are a language variant's, and
       nothing in part 1 says which duplicate is a library's file standing behind the app's.

       Both callers - the report and the dashboard line - come through ShadowCopiesFrom, so the two
       can never disagree about what counts as one. It answers rows of tShadowCopy, one per copy.

       PART 4 AND ITS KIND LEFT ON 2026-10-05. Nils, looking at the Rename dialog: "It is actually
       perfectly OK with duplicate filenames, as long as they are not a DataFlex system package. Thus
       all other 'duplicates' should be removed from the dialog" - and, asked about the report: "Yes!"
       So ShadowCopiesFrom answers the copies of DataFlex system packages and nothing else, and the
       board's line, its dialog and this report list those only. What is said above about the
       library-file copies is why they were listed for three weeks, not what the code does now -
       apart from ONE shape since 2026-11-12, a copy compiled in place of the file of a package that
       has errors in the same build (FailingPackageCopies).

       THE LISTING IS HISTORY; THE DISK IS NOW (Nils 2026-08-31). Every class-0 row was read out of
       a .prn, so it says which copy a PAST build compiled. After [Rename them] has moved a copy to
       <name>.shadowed the listing still names it - and this used to keep reporting it, so the
       dashboard line survived the very fix that cleared it and the button had nothing left to do.
       So a winner that is NO LONGER ON DISK is not a live override: it cannot win the next build and
       there is nothing to rename. It is counted out through iRetiredGone instead, because it is not
       nothing either - it means THIS listing predates the fix, which is exactly what the board has
       to say.

       AND THE COPIES THE BUILD NEVER READ (Nils 2026-09-13). The trigger above was "the compiler
       included YOUR copy", read from the listing - and a copy in a folder the compiler never
       searches passes it untouched, for ever. Those are class 1 in the same rows, judged by
       CopiesAgainstReference against the sweep of the home, offered the same rename - which for
       them changes nothing this build compiled. iClass says which is which; the board, the dialog
       and the report read it to word each one honestly.

       AND ONE EXCEPTION TO THE RULE OF 2026-10-05 (2026-11-12): a copy compiled in place of the file
       of a package that has errors in this build - FailingPackageCopies, the rows of kind
       eShadowFailingPackage. asErrFiles, the files the listing's ERROR lines name, is what it needs. */
    Function ShadowCopiesFrom String[] ByRef asLeaf String[] ByRef asWinner String sHome String[] ByRef asAll ;
            String[] ByRef asErrFiles tShadowCopy[] ByRef aRows Integer ByRef iRetiredGone Returns Integer
        String[] asShipped asOutLeaf asOutPath asOutShipped
        Integer[] aiClass aiErrors aiNone
        String sInstall
        Integer iCount i

        Move (ResizeArray(aRows, 0)) to aRows
        Move 0 to iRetiredGone
        // the install kind, when a target install is known
        Get psTargetPkgFolder of ghoApplication to sInstall
        If (Trim(sInstall) <> "") Begin
            Get InstallShippedNames sInstall to asShipped
            Get InstallCopiesClassified (&asLeaf) (&asWinner) (&asAll) (&asShipped) sHome sInstall ;
                (&asOutLeaf) (&asOutPath) (&asOutShipped) (&aiClass) to iCount
            Send _AppendShadowRows (&aRows) (&asOutLeaf) (&asOutPath) (&asOutShipped) (&aiClass) eShadowInstall (&iRetiredGone) (&aiNone)
        End
        // A copy of a file one of the workspace's libraries ships is no row since 2026-10-05 (see the
        // note above) - unless this build compiled it and that package fails in the same build.
        Get FailingPackageCopies (&asLeaf) (&asWinner) (&asAll) (&asErrFiles) sHome ;
            (&asOutLeaf) (&asOutPath) (&asOutShipped) (&aiErrors) to iCount
        If (iCount > 0) Begin
            Move (ResizeArray(aiClass, 0)) to aiClass
            For i from 0 to (iCount - 1)
                Move 0 to aiClass[i]
            Loop
            Send _AppendShadowRows (&aRows) (&asOutLeaf) (&asOutPath) (&asOutShipped) (&aiClass) eShadowFailingPackage (&iRetiredGone) (&aiErrors)
        End
        Function_Return (SizeOfArray(aRows))
    End_Function

    /* One classified set into the rows, with the two facts only the disk can answer: a class-0
       copy the listing named may have been moved away since (counted out through iRetiredGone),
       and whether the copy and the shipped file hold the same bytes - which is also the tick's
       default, because an identical copy is the one case a rename loses nothing. A path already
       in the rows (a file both the install and a package ship) is not added a second time.
       aiErrors, parallel to the rest, is the package's error count for eShadowFailingPackage; the
       install kind passes none. */
    Procedure _AppendShadowRows tShadowCopy[] ByRef aRows String[] ByRef asLeaf String[] ByRef asPath ;
            String[] ByRef asShipped Integer[] ByRef aiClass Integer eKind Integer ByRef iRetiredGone Integer[] ByRef aiErrors
        tShadowCopy Row
        tKeptShadow[] aKept
        Integer i iLast j jLast
        Boolean bStillThere bShippedThere bDup bSetting

        Get ReadKeptShadows to aKept
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLeaf) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            // A class-0 winner the listing named: still there, or moved away since? A class-1 copy
            // came off the live sweep, so it is there by construction.
            Move True to bStillThere
            If (aiClass[i] = 0) ;
                File_Exist asPath[i] bStillThere
            If (bStillThere = False) Begin
                Increment iRetiredGone
            End
            Else Begin
                Move False to bDup
                Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to jLast
                For j from 0 to jLast
                    If (Lowercase(Trim(aRows[j].sPath)) = Lowercase(Trim(asPath[i]))) ;
                        Move True to bDup
                Loop
                // A language setting is no outdated copy - see IsLanguageSettingLeaf.
                Get _SetsALanguage asLeaf[i] asPath[i] to bSetting
                If (bDup = False and bSetting = False) Begin
                    Get ShadowRowFrom asLeaf[i] asPath[i] asShipped[i] eKind aiClass[i] to Row
                    If (eKind = eShadowFailingPackage) Begin
                        Move (PoolPackageDisplayNameOf(Row.sShipped)) to Row.sSource
                        If (i < SizeOfArray(aiErrors)) ;
                            Move aiErrors[i] to Row.iPackageErrors
                    End
                    File_Exist Row.sShipped bShippedThere
                    If (bShippedThere = True) ;
                        Get _SameFileContent Row.sPath Row.sShipped to Row.bSame
                    Get IsAlwaysRetireFile Row.sLeaf to Row.bAlways
                    Move (Row.bSame or Row.bAlways) to Row.bTicked
                    // A copy the user decided to keep stays a row - the report and [Which files?]
                    // still name it - but it is off the line and out of the dialog until un-kept.
                    // A Get, not an expression: IsKeptPath is declared further down the class, and
                    // DataFlex resolves an expression call at the point of use.
                    Get IsKeptPath Row.sPath (&aKept) to Row.bKept
                    If (Row.bKept = True) ;
                        Move False to Row.bTicked
                    Move Row to aRows[SizeOfArray(aRows)]
                End
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    /* The same answer, for a caller that has not read the listing itself - the dashboard. Returns 0
       when there is no listing, which is the honest answer rather than a guess: which copy wins is a
       fact about a BUILD. */
    Function ShadowCopiesNow tShadowCopy[] ByRef aRows Integer ByRef iRetiredGone Returns Integer
        String[] asListing asLeaf asWinner asAll asErrFiles
        String sHome sListing sPath sLeaf
        Integer i iLast iIdx

        Get psHomeTarget of ghoApplication to sHome
        Get NewestListingFile sHome to sListing
        Move (ResizeArray(aRows, 0)) to aRows
        Move 0 to iRetiredGone     // defined on EVERY exit, including the no-listing one
        If (sListing = "") ;
            Function_Return 0
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sListing)) to asListing
        Move (SizeOfArray(asListing) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Get IncludedFileFromPrnLine asListing[i] (&sPath) to sLeaf
            If (sLeaf <> "") Begin
                Move (SearchArray(sLeaf, asLeaf)) to iIdx
                If (iIdx = -1) Begin
                    Move sLeaf to asLeaf[SizeOfArray(asLeaf)]
                    Move sPath to asWinner[SizeOfArray(asWinner)]
                End
            End
            Else Begin
                // the files this build's errors are in - which packages fail (FailingPackageCopies)
                Get ErrorFileFromPrnLine asListing[i] to sPath
                If (sPath <> "") ;
                    Move sPath to asErrFiles[SizeOfArray(asErrFiles)]
            End
        Loop
        // The sweep is what finds a copy the listing never mentions - once per memo, like the report.
        Get WorkspaceSourceFiles sHome to asAll
        Function_Return (ShadowCopiesFrom(Self, (&asLeaf), (&asWinner), sHome, (&asAll), (&asErrFiles), (&aRows), (&iRetiredGone)))
    End_Function



    /* WHERE THE KEPT LIST LIVES: Data\KeptShadows-<wskey>.json, in DFRefactor's own Data folder -
       never in the target workspace. Same fold and same folder as the analyzer's ignore list, whose
       path build this borrows: take the saved-plan path (the one source of truth on
       ghoApplication) and swap the file base. Both bases come from their CS_*Json Defines, so a
       rename of either constant stays consistent here. */
    Function KeptShadowsJsonPath Returns String
        String sPath sSavedBase sKeptBase

        /* A TESTABLE SEAM, and it is not optional here. Under UnitTests ghoApplication is a
           plain cApplication, so SavedPlanJsonPath COMPILES and returns "" - the silent-empty trap
           that turns a fixture green while it exercises nothing. psKeptShadowsFile lets a test
           point the round-trip at a scratch file and actually assert on it; production never sets
           it. See [[feedback_test_runner_app_class]]. */
        Get psKeptShadowsFile to sPath
        If (sPath <> "") ;
            Function_Return sPath
        Get SavedPlanJsonPath of ghoApplication to sPath
        If (sPath = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Left(CS_SavedPlanJson,   (Length(CS_SavedPlanJson)   - 5))) to sSavedBase   // "LastPlan"
        Move (Left(CS_KeptShadowsJson, (Length(CS_KeptShadowsJson) - 5))) to sKeptBase    // "KeptShadows"
        Function_Return (Replaces(sSavedBase, sPath, sKeptBase))
    End_Function

    // The copies this workspace's user decided to keep. Empty when absent / unparseable / written
    // by an older layout (iVersion <> CI_KeptShadowsVersion). Mirrors cModAnalyzer.ReadIgnored.
    Function ReadKeptShadows Returns tKeptShadow[]
        Handle hoJson
        tKeptShadowFile TheFile
        tKeptShadow[] aEmpty
        String sFile

        Get KeptShadowsJsonPath to sFile
        If (sFile = "") ;
            Function_Return aEmpty
        Get rfParseJsonFile sFile to hoJson
        If (hoJson = 0) ;
            Function_Return aEmpty
        Get JsonToDataType of hoJson to TheFile
        Send Destroy of hoJson
        If (TheFile.iVersion <> CI_KeptShadowsVersion) ;
            Function_Return aEmpty
        Function_Return TheFile.aRows
    End_Function

    // Persist it (pretty, NO BOM - a BOM breaks ParseUtf8 on the way back in).
    Procedure WriteKeptShadows tKeptShadow[] aRows
        Handle hoJson
        UChar[] ucJson
        Integer iCh
        String sFile
        tKeptShadowFile TheFile

        Get KeptShadowsJsonPath to sFile
        If (sFile = "") ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move CI_KeptShadowsVersion to TheFile.iVersion
        Move aRows to TheFile.aRows
        Get Create (RefClass(cJsonObject)) to hoJson
        Send DataTypeToJson of hoJson TheFile
        Set peWhiteSpace of hoJson to jpWhitespace_Pretty
        Get StringifyUtf8 of hoJson to ucJson
        Send Destroy of hoJson
        Get rfOpenOutput sFile to iCh
        If (iCh < 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Write channel iCh ucJson
        Send rfCloseOutput iCh
    End_Procedure

    /* PURE. Is this path one the user decided to keep, given the record? Case-insensitive, because
       DataFlex string compare is - which is right here, since Windows hides filename case anyway. */
    Function IsKeptPath String sPath tKeptShadow[] ByRef aKept Returns Boolean
        Integer i iLast

        Move (SizeOfArray(aKept) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Trim(aKept[i].sPath) = Trim(sPath)) ;
                Function_Return True
        Loop
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    // Has the user decided to keep this exact path? The record, read fresh.
    Function IsKeptShadow String sPath Returns Boolean
        tKeptShadow[] aKept

        Get ReadKeptShadows to aKept
        Function_Return (IsKeptPath(Self, sPath, (&aKept)))
    End_Function

    // Record a keep (idempotent - a second call for the same path changes nothing). Written ONLY
    // by a press: the dialog's "keep the rest" - the one deliberate act; see the note in
    // RefactorConstants - or the board's "Stay in <language>" for a retired language setting.
    Procedure RememberKept String sPath String sLeaf
        tKeptShadow[] aKept
        tKeptShadow Row

        Get ReadKeptShadows to aKept
        If (IsKeptPath(Self, sPath, (&aKept)) = True) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move sPath to Row.sPath
        Move sLeaf to Row.sLeaf
        Move Row to aKept[SizeOfArray(aKept)]
        Send WriteKeptShadows aKept
    End_Procedure

    // Forget one, so the line may offer it again. The "N kept" chip's way back.
    Procedure ForgetKept String sPath
        tKeptShadow[] aKept aOut
        Integer i iLast

        Get ReadKeptShadows to aKept
        Move (SizeOfArray(aKept) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Trim(aKept[i].sPath) <> Trim(sPath)) ;
                Move aKept[i] to aOut[SizeOfArray(aOut)]
        Loop
        Send WriteKeptShadows aOut
    End_Procedure

    /* PURE. The folders of a search path that are the workspace's own source, in search order. The
       path also carries the libraries, DFRefactor's own folders and DataFlex's. */
    Function OwnFoldersOnSearchPath String sSearchPath String sHome Returns String[]
        String[] asAll asOut
        String sFolder
        Integer i iLast

        Move (StrSplitToArray(sSearchPath, ";")) to asAll
        Move (SizeOfArray(asAll) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Trim(asAll[i])) to sFolder
            If (sFolder <> "") Begin
                If (IsWorkspaceOwnSource(Self, (vFolderFormat(sFolder)), sHome) = True) ;
                    Move sFolder to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // The retired language setting in one folder, as the disk spells it: <file>.shadowed, or the
    // lowest number when only numbered ones are left. "" when there is none.
    Function _RetiredLanguageFileIn String sFolder Returns String
        tRFSearchResult[] aFound
        String[] asNames
        Integer i iLast

        Move (rfFileSearch((vFolderFormat(sFolder) + CS_LanguageSettingFile + ".shadowed*"), DIRMODE_FILES_ONLY, False)) to aFound
        Move (SizeOfArray(aFound) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (Trim(aFound[i].sFilename) <> "") ;
                Move (Trim(aFound[i].sFilename)) to asNames[SizeOfArray(asNames)]
        Loop
        If (SizeOfArray(asNames) = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (SortArray(asNames)) to asNames
        Function_Return (vFolderFormat(sFolder) + asNames[0])
    End_Function

    // Is a file of this name in any of these folders?
    Function _IsFileInFolders String sLeaf String[] asFolders Returns Boolean
        String sPath
        Integer i iLast
        Boolean bThere

        Move (SizeOfArray(asFolders) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (vFolderFormat(asFolders[i]) + sLeaf) to sPath
            File_Exist sPath bThere
            If (bThere = True) ;
                Function_Return True
        Loop
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    /* A LANGUAGE SETTING [Rename them] ALREADY TOOK AWAY (Nils 2026-11-05, asked whether the board
       should offer it back: yes). From 2026-09-13 until the rule at IsLanguageSettingLeaf the dialog
       could rename a workspace's Language_Current.inc, and the programs went on compiling without
       an error, in another language, with the file out of sight as <name>.shadowed.

       Offered only when renaming it back would do what the offer says, which is why each test is here:

         - no live Language_Current.inc in the folders given: that one is the answer now
         - its folder is on the search path: the compiler never read one anywhere else, so the rename
           took nothing away (the caller passes the workspace's own folders on the path)
         - it names a language and includes its texts: the Define-only form is the broken one
         - that is not the install's language: then the rename changed nothing
         - the file it includes can be found: measured, 238 errors if not
         - nobody chose to stay with the install's language (RememberKept, the board's other answer)

       At most one answer, the first in search order, because that is the one that would win. Fills
       sLanguage and returns the file's path, or returns "". */
    Function RetiredLanguageSettingIn String[] asFolders String sInstallFolder String sInstallLanguage String ByRef sLanguage Returns String
        tKeptShadow[] aKept
        String[] asLines asLook
        String sRetired sPicked sInclude
        Integer i iLast
        Boolean bReach bKept

        Move "" to sLanguage
        If (_IsFileInFolders(Self, CS_LanguageSettingFile, asFolders) = True) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move asFolders to asLook
        Move sInstallFolder to asLook[SizeOfArray(asLook)]
        Get ReadKeptShadows to aKept
        Move (SizeOfArray(asFolders) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Get _RetiredLanguageFileIn asFolders[i] to sRetired
            If (sRetired <> "") Begin
                Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sRetired)) to asLines
                Get LanguageSettingOf (&asLines) (&sInclude) to sPicked
                Get IsKeptPath sRetired (&aKept) to bKept
                Get _IsFileInFolders sInclude asLook to bReach
                If (sPicked <> "" and Lowercase(sPicked) <> Lowercase(sInstallLanguage) and bKept = False and bReach = True) Begin
                    Move sPicked to sLanguage
                    Function_Return sRetired
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    /* The same answer for the board: sSearchPath is the target workspace's composite path, and the
       language it is compared with is the one the install's own Language_Current.inc picks. No
       install known, or one that sets no language: no offer, since the sentence could not be true. */
    Function RetiredLanguageSettingNow String sSearchPath String ByRef sLanguage String ByRef sInstallLanguage Returns String
        String[] asFolders asLines
        String sHome sInstall sInclude

        Move "" to sLanguage
        Move "" to sInstallLanguage
        Get psHomeTarget of ghoApplication to sHome
        Get psTargetPkgFolder of ghoApplication to sInstall
        If (Trim(sHome) = "" or Trim(sInstall) = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(vFolderFormat(sInstall) + CS_LanguageSettingFile)) to asLines
        Get LanguageSettingOf (&asLines) (&sInclude) to sInstallLanguage
        If (sInstallLanguage = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Get OwnFoldersOnSearchPath sSearchPath sHome to asFolders
        Function_Return (RetiredLanguageSettingIn(Self, asFolders, sInstall, sInstallLanguage, (&sLanguage)))
    End_Function

    // PURE. The live name a retired language setting goes back to, in its own folder.
    Function LiveLanguageSettingPath String sRetired Returns String
        Integer iAt

        Move (RightPos(CS_DirSeparator, sRetired)) to iAt
        If (iAt = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (Left(sRetired, iAt) + CS_LanguageSettingFile)
    End_Function

    // Renames it back. "" when done, else the reason. rfRenameFile refuses to overwrite, so a live
    // setting that turned up since the board was drawn is left as it is.
    Function RestoreLanguageSetting String sRetired Returns String
        String sLive

        Get LiveLanguageSettingPath sRetired to sLive
        If (sLive = "") ;
            Function_Return ("not a path this may rename: " + sRetired)
        Function_Return (rfRenameFile(sRetired, sLive))
    End_Function

    /* RETIRE the workspace copies the user ticked - the [Rename them] the board offers (Nils
       2026-08-30: "a concise line explaining it and a button with a [Fix it] type of thing, that
       renames those offending local copies").

       WHICH ONES IS THE USER'S CALL, ROW BY ROW, since 2026-09-15: the rows arrive from the dialog
       (RetireShadowsFT.dg) with bTicked set, and only a ticked row is touched. The dialog ticks an
       identical copy and leaves a DIFFERENT one unticked, because measured on five workspaces
       every library-file copy differed from the library's - each a fork until someone looks - and
       that is Nils's call ("we probably need to suggest this on a file-by-file basis"). It replaced
       two earlier shapes, both his calls in their day: retire every override behind one confirm
       (2026-08-30), and skip for ever a copy found live again after a retire (dropped 2026-09-15 -
       a REVERT puts a file back too, and the skipped copies stayed in front of the shipped file for
       every other program while the row kept offering a press with nothing to do).

       Both halves of the safety are built in, whatever is ticked:

         - BACKED UP FIRST, then RENAMED - never deleted - to <name>.shadowed. Two undo paths, and
           they are not redundant: Revert restores from the backup folder (the app's own undo, and
           the one a user reaches for), while renaming the .shadowed twin back works even if this
           program never runs again. A file whose backup fails is LEFT ALONE, exactly as the engine
           leaves a file it could not back up. rfRenameFile also refuses to overwrite, so an earlier
           retire's twin is never destroyed by a later one - and since 2026-09-14 a later retire takes
           the next free NUMBERED name (ShadowTargetName) instead of failing on that twin.
         - A copy can be a DELIBERATE FORK. Retiring MonthCalendarPrompt.dg on the workspace this
           was built for BREAKS the build - the install copy declares oMonthCalendarPrompt while the
           app calls oCalendar - and Prnt_dlg.pkg has form: three guards there produced 543 errors
           on 2026-08-26 ([[feedback_guard_must_not_remove_what_the_file_calls]]). The dialog shows
           the content verdict per row and starts a different copy unticked; the board says REBUILD
           afterwards, because the effect of a retire is invisible until the compiler runs again.

       Returns how many were renamed. asFailed comes back holding one "leaf - reason" line per
       ticked file that could not be renamed; asTwins one line per file that took a NUMBERED name
       because an earlier twin was there, saying whether that twin is identical; iLiveDone the
       class-0 renames, the only ones the next compile can feel. A partial result is normal and is
       reported, never rolled back - rolling back would undo renames that succeeded and are wanted. */
    Function RetireShadowCopies tShadowCopy[] ByRef aRows String[] ByRef asFailed String[] ByRef asTwins Integer ByRef iLiveDone Returns Integer
        String[] asTaken
        String sWhy sTo sPlain sToLeaf sLeaf sPath
        Boolean bOk bSame
        Integer i iLast iDone

        Move (ResizeArray(asFailed, 0)) to asFailed
        Move (ResizeArray(asTwins, 0)) to asTwins
        Move 0 to iDone
        Move 0 to iLiveDone
        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (aRows[i].bTicked = True) Begin
                Move aRows[i].sLeaf to sLeaf
                Move aRows[i].sPath to sPath
                /* BACK UP FIRST, AND DO NOT TOUCH THE FILE IF THAT FAILS (Nils 2026-08-30: "Are
                   you saying that the [Rename them] doesn't take a backup first? if so, that is a
                   bug"). It is the engine's contract for every other write this app makes - see
                   the SaveBackupFile call in cRefactorEngine, which returns eEngineBackupErr and
                   changes nothing when the copy fails - and a retire had been skipping it.

                   "The .shadowed twin is already the backup" was the wrong answer. It is safe
                   from DATA LOSS, but it is not the app's undo: Revert reads the backup FOLDER,
                   so a retire nothing had backed up was the one change this tool could make that
                   its own Revert could not take back. It also left the only copy sitting in the
                   user's source tree, where a tidy-up or a VCS clean can take it. */
                Get SaveBackupFile of ghoApplication sPath to bOk
                If (bOk = False) Begin
                    Move (sLeaf + " - could not be copied to the backup area, so it was left alone") ;
                        to asFailed[SizeOfArray(asFailed)]
                End
                Else Begin
                    // The first free twin name: <file>.shadowed, or numbered past the ones there.
                    Get _ShadowNamesTaken sPath to asTaken
                    Get ShadowTargetName sPath asTaken to sTo
                    If (sTo = "") Begin
                        Move (sLeaf + " - every .shadowed name up to 99 is already taken beside it") ;
                            to asFailed[SizeOfArray(asFailed)]
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        Move (rfRenameFile(sPath, sTo)) to sWhy
                        If (sWhy = "") Begin
                            Increment iDone
                            If (aRows[i].iClass = 0) ;
                                Increment iLiveDone
                            /* A NUMBERED NAME SAYS WHY, and whether the older twin still matters: a
                               Revert brings back the same bytes, so the two are usually identical and
                               the older twin is redundant; when they differ the reader is told to look
                               before retiring the older one by hand. Neither is deleted here. */
                            Move (sPath + ".shadowed") to sPlain
                            If (Lowercase(sTo) <> Lowercase(sPlain)) Begin
                                Get _SameFileContent sTo sPlain to bSame
                                Move (Right(sTo, (Length(sTo) - RightPos(CS_DirSeparator, sTo)))) to sToLeaf
                                If (bSame = True) ;
                                    Move (sLeaf + " - renamed to " + sToLeaf + "; an earlier " + sLeaf ;
                                        + ".shadowed was already there, identical to this copy, and is kept") ;
                                        to asTwins[SizeOfArray(asTwins)]
                                Else ;
                                    Move (sLeaf + " - renamed to " + sToLeaf + "; an earlier " + sLeaf ;
                                        + ".shadowed was already there, DIFFERENT from this copy, and is kept - compare" ;
                                        + " the two before retiring the older one by hand") to asTwins[SizeOfArray(asTwins)]
                            End
                        End
                        Else ;
                            Move (sLeaf + " - " + sWhy) to asFailed[SizeOfArray(asFailed)]
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return iDone
    End_Function


    /* PART 2 - the library FOLDER a migration left behind, which is where most shadowed files come
       from. Returns how many were found; writes its own section.

       Nils, 2026-08-30, after finding Libraries\VDFQuery beside the VDFQuery20 package: "I had
       removed the DUF as a library, and added it as a package. But the DUF library is still there
       on disk." The Libraries dialog edits the .sws, which is its job - deleting a folder would be
       a surprising and irreversible side effect of a list edit - so nothing said the old tree was
       still there, still on the search path, and still able to win.

       TWO SIGNALS, BOTH REQUIRED, because either alone lies. The listing says nothing from the
       folder was COMPILED - but a library used only by another project in the workspace would fail
       that test innocently. The .sws text says nothing DECLARES it - but a declared folder can sit
       unused. Reported only when both agree.

       AND IT NEVER OFFERS TO DELETE. Measured on that workspace, the stale trees were not copies
       of their packages at all: Libraries\DUF held 154 source files, 16 matching the package, 49
       differing, and 86 present nowhere in it. Whatever those 86 are - an older bundled
       sub-library, or a local patch someone made years ago - they are not the tool's to discard.
       The report states the numbers and prints a rename the user can run and undo. */
    Function _StaleLibraryFolders String sHome String[] ByRef asListing Integer iCh Returns Integer
        tRFSearchResult[] aDirs
        String  sLibRoot sName sDir sSws sPkg sLowDir
        Integer i iLast iFound iSame iDiffer iOnlyHere iLine iLineLast
        Boolean bCompiled

        Move (vFolderFormat(sHome) + "Libraries") to sLibRoot
        Move (rfFileSearch((vFolderFormat(sLibRoot) + "*.*"), DIRMODE_DIRECTORIES_ONLY, False)) to aDirs
        Move (SizeOfArray(aDirs) - 1) to iLast
        If (iLast < 0) ;
            Function_Return 0
        Get SwsDeclarationText sHome to sSws
        Move 0 to iFound
        Move (SizeOfArray(asListing) - 1) to iLineLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (Trim(aDirs[i].sFilename)) to sName
            If (sName <> "" and sName <> "." and sName <> "..") Begin
                Move (vFolderFormat(sLibRoot) + sName) to sDir
                Move (Lowercase(CS_DirSeparator + "libraries" + CS_DirSeparator + Lowercase(sName) + CS_DirSeparator)) to sLowDir
                // Did anything under it reach the compiler?
                Move False to bCompiled
                For iLine from 0 to iLineLast
                    If (Lowercase(asListing[iLine]) contains sLowDir) Begin
                        Move True to bCompiled
                        Move iLineLast to iLine
                    End
                Loop
                If (bCompiled = False and (not(sSws contains (Lowercase("libraries/" + sName))))) Begin
                    If (not(sSws contains (Lowercase("libraries" + CS_DirSeparator + sName)))) Begin
                        If (iFound = 0) Begin
                            Writeln channel iCh ""
                            Writeln channel iCh "=== Library folders the workspace no longer uses ==="
                            Writeln channel iCh "Nothing under these was compiled into this program, and no .sws mentions them."
                            Writeln channel iCh "Typically what a move to git packages leaves behind - the package supplies the"
                            Writeln channel iCh "library now, and the old tree stays on disk where it can still win the search path."
                            Writeln channel iCh ""
                        End
                        Increment iFound
                        Writeln channel iCh ("=== " + sName + " ===")
                        Writeln channel iCh ("  folder        : " + sDir)
                        Get PackageFolderFor sHome sName to sPkg
                        If (sPkg <> "") Begin
                            Send FolderVersusPackage sDir sPkg (&iSame) (&iDiffer) (&iOnlyHere)
                            Writeln channel iCh ("  replaced by   : " + sPkg)
                            Writeln channel iCh ("  source files  : " + String(iSame) + " same size as the package, " ;
                                + String(iDiffer) + " differ, " + String(iOnlyHere) + " exist ONLY here")
                            If (iOnlyHere > 0) ;
                                Writeln channel iCh ("  READ THIS     : " + String(iOnlyHere) + " file(s) are in no form in the package - check what they are before removing anything.")
                        End
                        Else ;
                            Writeln channel iCh "  replaced by   : no matching package found - this may be a library you removed on purpose."
                        Writeln channel iCh ("  to retire it  : ren " + '"' + sDir + '" "' + sName + '.OLD"')
                        Writeln channel iCh "                  (a rename, so a compile proves nothing needed it; rename back to undo)"
                        Writeln channel iCh ""
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return iFound
    End_Function

    /* ---- WHAT A DIFFERENT COPY ADDS, AND WHETHER ANYTHING USES IT (Nils 2026-11-12) ----

       A copy that differs from the file it stands in front of starts unticked: it may be a fork. Nils,
       on 2026-11-12, of a copy whose additions nothing in the workspace uses: it comes TICKED. Measured on
       a workspace's 1998 copy of Prnt_dlg.pkg (2026-11-01): it differed by 268 lines and added a property,
       two methods and two Types that neither the shipped file nor the packages it Uses declare; nothing in
       the workspace used any of them, and renamed, its 608 errors went and none came from it.

       WHAT "ADDS" MEANS: a name the copy declares (DeclaredNamesOf) that neither the shipped file nor a
       file it Uses declares (ShippedNamesOf). WHAT "USES" MEANS (NameUseOnLine): the name in any other
       source file under the workspace, comments left out, as a whole word - and a name declared inside a
       Class only as a message: Get / Send / Set X, X(Self, msg_X / get_X / set_X, or a method of that
       name elsewhere. A copy's method can share its name with a DataFlex built-in function the workspace
       calls everywhere; Prnt_dlg.pkg's PointerToString did.

       WHAT IT CANNOT SEE: a change INSIDE a method both files have. A copy that only edits method bodies
       adds nothing, so it is ticked too - Nils's call, with that said. A copy in which no declaration is
       found at all (a menu built by DFCreate_Menu) tells nothing either way and stays unticked. A rename
       is reversible, and a name that turns out to be used fails the next compile. */

    // PURE. Is c, one character of an uppercased line, part of a name?
    Function _IsNameChar String c Returns Boolean
        If (c = "") ;
            Function_Return False
        Function_Return (Pos(c, "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_#$@") > 0)
    End_Function

    // PURE. Does sLine (uppercased) hold sWord as a whole word? A dot in front makes it a field's name.
    Function _HasWord String sLine String sWord Returns Boolean
        String sRest sBefore sAfter
        Integer iAt iLen

        Move (Length(sWord)) to iLen
        If (iLen = 0) ;
            Function_Return False
        Move sLine to sRest
        Move (Pos(sWord, sRest)) to iAt
        While (iAt > 0)
            Move "" to sBefore
            If (iAt > 1) ;
                Move (Mid(sRest, 1, (iAt - 1))) to sBefore
            Move (Mid(sRest, 1, (iAt + iLen))) to sAfter
            If (_IsNameChar(Self, sBefore) = False and sBefore <> "." and _IsNameChar(Self, sAfter) = False) ;
                Function_Return True
            Move (Right(sRest, (Length(sRest) - iAt))) to sRest
            Move (Pos(sWord, sRest)) to iAt
        Loop
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    // PURE. The words of a line, tabs as spaces, no empty ones.
    Function _Words String sLine Returns String[]
        String[] asAll asOut
        Integer i iLast

        Move (StrSplitToArray(Trim(Replaces(Character(9), sLine, " ")), " ")) to asAll
        Move (SizeOfArray(asAll) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (asAll[i] <> "") ;
                Move asAll[i] to asOut[SizeOfArray(asOut)]
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // PURE. The lines with their comments blanked: from // to the end of a line, and block comments across
    // lines. A comment marker inside a string is cut too - that only ever hides a name, never adds one.
    Function _CodeOnlyLines String[] ByRef asLines Returns String[]
        String[] asOut
        String sLine
        Integer i iLast iAt iBlock iEnd
        Boolean bBlock

        Move False to bBlock
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move asLines[i] to sLine
            If (bBlock = True) Begin
                Move (Pos("*/", sLine)) to iEnd
                If (iEnd = 0) ;
                    Move "" to sLine
                Else Begin
                    Move (Right(sLine, (Length(sLine) - iEnd - 1))) to sLine
                    Move False to bBlock
                End
            End
            If (bBlock = False) Begin
                Move (Pos("//", sLine)) to iAt
                Move (Pos("/*", sLine)) to iBlock
                If (iBlock > 0 and (iAt = 0 or iBlock < iAt)) Begin
                    Move (Pos("*/", Right(sLine, (Length(sLine) - iBlock - 1)))) to iEnd
                    If (iEnd = 0) Begin
                        Move (Left(sLine, (iBlock - 1))) to sLine
                        Move True to bBlock
                    End
                    Else ;
                        Move (Left(sLine, (iBlock - 1)) + " " + Right(sLine, (Length(sLine) - iBlock - iEnd - 2))) to sLine
                    Move (Pos("//", sLine)) to iAt
                End
                If (iAt > 0) ;
                    Move (Left(sLine, (iAt - 1))) to sLine
            End
            Move sLine to asOut[i]
        Loop
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // Uppercased into the list, once.
    Procedure _AddUpperOnce String[] ByRef asList String sName
        Move (Uppercase(Trim(sName))) to sName
        If (sName <> "" and SearchArray(sName, asList) = -1) ;
            Move sName to asList[SizeOfArray(asList)]
    End_Procedure

    /* PURE. What a source file DECLARES, by a line's first word: Class, Procedure (Procedure Set X gives
       X), Function, Object, Define, #REPLACE, Property (its name is the third word), Struct, Type,
       #COMMAND and External_Function - uppercased, once each, comments left out. A Procedure, Function or
       Property inside a Class goes to asMethods too: it is used as a message (NameUseOnLine). */
    Procedure DeclaredNamesOf String[] ByRef asLines String[] ByRef asNames String[] ByRef asMethods
        String[] asCode asWords
        String sFirst sName
        Integer i iLast iDepth iWords

        Move (ResizeArray(asNames, 0))   to asNames
        Move (ResizeArray(asMethods, 0)) to asMethods
        Get _CodeOnlyLines (&asLines) to asCode
        Move 0 to iDepth
        Move (SizeOfArray(asCode) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Get _Words asCode[i] to asWords
            Move (SizeOfArray(asWords)) to iWords
            If (iWords > 0) Begin
                Move (Lowercase(asWords[0])) to sFirst
                Move "" to sName
                If (sFirst = "class" and iWords > 1) Begin
                    Move asWords[1] to sName
                    Increment iDepth
                End
                Else If (sFirst = "end_class") Begin
                    If (iDepth > 0) ;
                        Decrement iDepth
                End
                Else If ((sFirst = "procedure" or sFirst = "function") and iWords > 1) Begin
                    Move asWords[1] to sName
                    If (sFirst = "procedure" and Lowercase(asWords[1]) = "set" and iWords > 2) ;
                        Move asWords[2] to sName
                    If (iDepth > 0) ;
                        Send _AddUpperOnce (&asMethods) sName
                End
                Else If (sFirst = "property" and iWords > 2) Begin
                    Move asWords[2] to sName
                    If (iDepth > 0) ;
                        Send _AddUpperOnce (&asMethods) sName
                End
                Else If (iWords > 1) Begin
                    If (sFirst = "object" or sFirst = "define" or sFirst = "#replace" or sFirst = "struct" or sFirst = "type" or sFirst = "#command" or sFirst = "external_function") ;
                        Move asWords[1] to sName
                End
                If (sName <> "") ;
                    Send _AddUpperOnce (&asNames) sName
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    /* The names the SHIPPED file stands for, SORTED: what it declares and what the files it Uses declare,
       looked up in its own folder and then the install's Pkg folder - at most 100 files. A copy declaring a
       Struct the shipped file gets from Dftypes.pkg adds nothing. */
    Function ShippedNamesOf String sShipped String sInstall Returns String[]
        String[] asQueue asSeen asLines asCode asWords asNames asMine asMethods
        String sPath sLeaf sTry sDir
        Integer iNext i iLast j jLast
        Boolean bThere

        Move (Trim(sShipped)) to asQueue[0]
        Move 0 to iNext
        While (iNext < SizeOfArray(asQueue) and SizeOfArray(asSeen) < 100)
            Move asQueue[iNext] to sPath
            Increment iNext
            If (SearchArray(Lowercase(sPath), asSeen) = -1) Begin
                Move (Lowercase(sPath)) to asSeen[SizeOfArray(asSeen)]
                File_Exist sPath bThere
                If (bThere = True) Begin
                    Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sPath)) to asLines
                    Send DeclaredNamesOf (&asLines) (&asMine) (&asMethods)
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asMine) - 1) to jLast
                    For j from 0 to jLast
                        If (SearchArray(asMine[j], asNames) = -1) ;
                            Move asMine[j] to asNames[SizeOfArray(asNames)]
                    Loop
                    Move (Left(sPath, RightPos("\", sPath))) to sDir
                    Get _CodeOnlyLines (&asLines) to asCode
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asCode) - 1) to iLast
                    For i from 0 to iLast
                        Get _Words asCode[i] to asWords
                        If (SizeOfArray(asWords) > 1) Begin
                            If (Lowercase(asWords[0]) = "use") Begin
                                Move (Replaces('"', asWords[1], "")) to sLeaf
                                Move (Replaces("'", sLeaf, "")) to sLeaf
                                If (Pos(".", ExtractFileName(sLeaf)) = 0) ;
                                    Move (sLeaf + ".pkg") to sLeaf
                                Move (sDir + sLeaf) to sTry
                                File_Exist sTry bThere
                                If (bThere = False and Trim(sInstall) <> "") Begin
                                    Move (vFolderFormat(sInstall) + sLeaf) to sTry
                                    File_Exist sTry bThere
                                End
                                If (bThere = True) ;
                                    Move sTry to asQueue[SizeOfArray(asQueue)]
                            End
                        End
                    Loop
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return (SortArray(asNames))
    End_Function

    /* PURE. Does sLine - uppercased, comments out, one space between words - use sName? A plain name: as a
       whole word. A method's (bMethod): only as a message - Get / Send / Set X, a method of that name,
       X(Self, or msg_X / get_X / set_X - so a call of a built-in function of the same name is no use. */
    Function NameUseOnLine String sLine String sName Boolean bMethod Returns Boolean
        If (bMethod = False) ;
            Function_Return (_HasWord(Self, sLine, sName))
        If (_HasWord(Self, sLine, ("GET " + sName)) or _HasWord(Self, sLine, ("SEND " + sName)) or _HasWord(Self, sLine, ("SET " + sName))) ;
            Function_Return True
        If (_HasWord(Self, sLine, ("PROCEDURE " + sName)) or _HasWord(Self, sLine, ("FUNCTION " + sName))) ;
            Function_Return True
        If (_HasWord(Self, sLine, (sName + "(SELF")) or _HasWord(Self, sLine, (sName + " (SELF"))) ;
            Function_Return True
        Function_Return (_HasWord(Self, sLine, ("MSG_" + sName)) or _HasWord(Self, sLine, ("GET_" + sName)) or _HasWord(Self, sLine, ("SET_" + sName)))
    End_Function

    /* Marks every DIFFERENT row - not identical, not an always-rename, not kept - whose copy declares
       something and adds no name anything else in the workspace uses: bAddsNothingUsed, and TICKED (Nils
       2026-11-12). asFiles is the sweep of the home (WorkspaceSourceFiles); a file is read line by line
       only when its text holds one of the added names at all. Returns the rows marked. */
    Function MarkCopiesThatAddNothingUsed tShadowCopy[] ByRef aRows String[] ByRef asFiles String sInstall Returns Integer
        String[] asCopyLines asMine asMethods asShipped asName asLines asCode
        Integer[] aiOwner
        Boolean[] abMethod abUsed abDeclares abCandidate
        String sText sLine sPathLow
        Integer i iLast j jLast k kLast iCount iFile iFileLast
        Boolean bThere bAny

        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to iLast
        // each candidate's added names, in one list with the row that owns each
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move False to abCandidate[i]
            Move False to abDeclares[i]
            If (aRows[i].bSame = False and aRows[i].bAlways = False and aRows[i].bKept = False) Begin
                File_Exist aRows[i].sPath bThere
                If (bThere = True) Begin
                    Move True to abCandidate[i]
                    Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(aRows[i].sPath)) to asCopyLines
                    Send DeclaredNamesOf (&asCopyLines) (&asMine) (&asMethods)
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asMine) > 0) to abDeclares[i]
                    Get ShippedNamesOf aRows[i].sShipped sInstall to asShipped
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asMine) - 1) to jLast
                    For j from 0 to jLast
                        If (BinarySearchArray(asMine[j], asShipped) = -1) Begin
                            Move asMine[j] to asName[SizeOfArray(asName)]
                            Move i         to aiOwner[SizeOfArray(aiOwner)]
                            Move (SearchArray(asMine[j], asMethods) <> -1) to abMethod[SizeOfArray(abMethod)]
                            Move False     to abUsed[SizeOfArray(abUsed)]
                        End
                    Loop
                End
            End
        Loop
        // one pass over the workspace's source for all of them
        Move (SizeOfArray(asName) - 1) to kLast
        If (kLast >= 0) Begin
            Move (SizeOfArray(asFiles) - 1) to iFileLast
            For iFile from 0 to iFileLast
                Move (Lowercase(Trim(asFiles[iFile]))) to sPathLow
                Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(asFiles[iFile])) to asLines
                Move (Uppercase(StrJoinFromArray(asLines, " "))) to sText
                Move False to bAny
                For k from 0 to kLast
                    If (abUsed[k] = False and Pos(asName[k], sText) > 0) Begin
                        If (Lowercase(Trim(aRows[aiOwner[k]].sPath)) <> sPathLow) ;
                            Move True to bAny
                    End
                Loop
                If (bAny = True) Begin
                    Get _CodeOnlyLines (&asLines) to asCode
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asCode) - 1) to jLast
                    For j from 0 to jLast
                        Move (Uppercase(Trim(Replaces(Character(9), asCode[j], " ")))) to sLine
                        If (sLine <> "") Begin
                            While (Pos("  ", sLine) > 0)
                                Move (Replaces("  ", sLine, " ")) to sLine
                            Loop
                            For k from 0 to kLast
                                If (abUsed[k] = False and Pos(asName[k], sLine) > 0) Begin
                                    If (Lowercase(Trim(aRows[aiOwner[k]].sPath)) <> sPathLow) Begin
                                        If (NameUseOnLine(Self, sLine, asName[k], abMethod[k]) = True) ;
                                            Move True to abUsed[k]
                                    End
                                End
                            Loop
                        End
                    Loop
                End
            Loop
        End
        // a row whose copy declares something and none of whose added names is used
        Move 0 to iCount
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (abCandidate[i] = True and abDeclares[i] = True) Begin
                Move False to bAny
                For k from 0 to kLast
                    If (aiOwner[k] = i and abUsed[k] = True) ;
                        Move True to bAny
                Loop
                If (bAny = False) Begin
                    Move True to aRows[i].bAddsNothingUsed
                    Move True to aRows[i].bTicked
                    Increment iCount
                End
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return iCount
    End_Function

    // PURE. The content verdict of one row, as the report prints it.
    Function _ContentVerdict tShadowCopy Row Returns String
        String sWhose

        Move "the shipped file" to sWhose
        If (Row.eKind = eShadowFailingPackage) ;
            Move "the package's file" to sWhose
        If (Row.bSame = True) ;
            Function_Return ("identical to " + sWhose)
        If (Row.bAddsNothingUsed = True) ;
            Function_Return ("DIFFERENT from " + sWhose + ", but nothing in the workspace uses a name it adds - ticked for a rename (a change inside a method both have is not seen)")
        Function_Return ("DIFFERENT from " + sWhose + " - compare the two before renaming")
    End_Function

    /* The report. Returns the number of shadowed files found.

       TWO SOURCES, because neither alone is enough. The listing says which copy WON - the
       compiler's own answer, which beats simulating the search path - but the losers never appear
       in it, precisely because they were not opened. The filesystem sweep supplies those. So:
       walk the listing for what was included, sweep the workspace for what else carries the same
       name, and report only where the two disagree.

       REPORT ONLY, and it always will be. A second copy of a package can be a deliberate local
       fork - a real workspace carried a hand-tweaked "..._ext.pkg" beside the original, with
       renamed functions, which had to stay - and no rule in a file name separates a fork from a
       leftover. Deleting or rewriting one is a decision only the reader can make. */
    Function FindShadowedPackageFiles Returns Integer
        String[] asListing asAll asShadows
        String[] asLeaf asWinner asErrFiles
        tShadowCopy[] aRows
        String   sHome sLogFile sListing sLine sPath sLeaf sPrev sInstall
        Integer  iCh iLine iLineLast iIdx i iLast j jLast iTotal iStale iShadows iInsGone iLive iDormant iFail iSafe
        Boolean  bPanel bCancel

        Get psHomeTarget of ghoApplication to sHome
        Move (vFolderFormat(sHome) + CS_BackupFolder + CS_DirSeparator + CS_ShadowedPackagesLogFile) to sLogFile
        Get rfOpenOutput sLogFile to iCh
        If (iCh < 0) ;
            Function_Return 0
        Set psLogFile to sLogFile

        Writeln channel iCh "Shadowed package files  (report only - no changes made)."
        Writeln channel iCh "Files that exist in more than one place under this workspace, and the copy the"
        Writeln channel iCh "compiler actually used. A stale copy compiles perfectly - that is the problem:"
        Writeln channel iCh "fix the library and the workspace keeps building the other file."
        Writeln channel iCh ""

        Move (ghoStatusPanel <> 0 and Active_State(ghoStatusPanel) = True) to bPanel
        Get NewestListingFile sHome to sListing
        Set psListingUsed to sListing
        If (sListing = "") Begin
            // NO EVIDENCE, so no verdict. Which copy wins is a fact about a build, and without a
            // listing there has been no build to read it from. Saying "these names are duplicated"
            // instead would be a different, far noisier report - and not the question asked.
            Writeln channel iCh "No compiler listing (.prn) was found under this workspace, so there is nothing"
            Writeln channel iCh "to read the resolution out of - which copy wins is a fact about a BUILD, not"
            Writeln channel iCh "about the folders. Compile the program once, then run this report again."
            Send rfCloseOutput iCh
            Function_Return 0
        End
        Writeln channel iCh ("Resolution read from: " + sListing)
        Writeln channel iCh ""

        If (bPanel = True) Begin
            Set Title_Text of ghoStatusPanel to "Reading the compiler listing:"
            Set TableName_Text of ghoStatusPanel to sListing
        End
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sListing)) to asListing
        Move (SizeOfArray(asListing)) to iLineLast
        If (bPanel = True) Begin
            Set piPosition of ghoProgressBar to 0
            Set piMaximum  of ghoProgressBar to iLineLast
        End
        Decrement iLineLast
        // PASS 1 - what the compile included, deduped by leaf. A package included from several
        // places in one build keeps its FIRST resolution: that is the one the search path gives.
        Move False to bCancel
        For iLine from 0 to iLineLast
            If (Mod(iLine, 500) = 0) Begin
                If (bPanel = True) Begin
                    Send Update_StatusPanel of ghoStatusPanel ("Listing line:" * String(iLine + 1) * "of:" * String(iLineLast + 1))
                    Set piPosition of ghoProgressBar to (iLine + 1)
                End
                Get pbUserCancelRequested of ghoEngine to bCancel
                If (bCancel = True) ;
                    Move iLineLast to iLine
            End
            Move asListing[iLine] to sLine
            Get IncludedFileFromPrnLine sLine (&sPath) to sLeaf
            If (sLeaf <> "") Begin
                Move (SearchArray(sLeaf, asLeaf)) to iIdx
                If (iIdx = -1) Begin
                    Move sLeaf to asLeaf[SizeOfArray(asLeaf)]
                    Move sPath to asWinner[SizeOfArray(asWinner)]
                End
            End
            Else Begin
                Get ErrorFileFromPrnLine sLine to sPath
                If (sPath <> "") ;
                    Move sPath to asErrFiles[SizeOfArray(asErrFiles)]
            End
        Loop

        // PASS 2 - every .pkg / .inc / .h under the workspace, so the copies that were NOT opened
        // can be seen at all.
        If (bCancel = False) Begin
            If (bPanel = True) Begin
                Set Title_Text of ghoStatusPanel to "Sweeping the workspace for copies:"
                Set TableName_Text of ghoStatusPanel to sHome
            End
            Get WorkspaceSourceFiles sHome to asAll
        End

        Move 0 to iTotal
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLeaf) - 1) to iLast
        If (bPanel = True) Begin
            Set piPosition of ghoProgressBar to 0
            Set piMaximum  of ghoProgressBar to (iLast + 1)
        End
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (bCancel = True) ;
                Move iLast to i
            If (Mod(i, 20) = 0) Begin
                If (bPanel = True) Begin
                    Send Update_StatusPanel of ghoStatusPanel ("Comparing:" * String(i + 1) * "of:" * String(iLast + 1))
                    Set piPosition of ghoProgressBar to (i + 1)
                End
                Get pbUserCancelRequested of ghoEngine to bCancel
            End
            Get ShadowCopiesOf asLeaf[i] asWinner[i] asAll to asShadows
            Move (SizeOfArray(asShadows) - 1) to jLast
            If (jLast >= 0) Begin
                Increment iTotal
                Writeln channel iCh ("=== " + asLeaf[i] + "  (" + String(jLast + 2) + " copies) ===")
                Writeln channel iCh ("  compiled from : " + asWinner[i])
                For j from 0 to jLast
                    If (j = 0) ;
                        Writeln channel iCh ("  also present  : " + asShadows[j])
                    Else ;
                        Writeln channel iCh ("                  " + asShadows[j])
                Loop
                Writeln channel iCh ""
            End
        Loop

        // ---- PART 3: the workspace overriding a file of DataFlex OWN. ----
        // FIRST in the log although it was added last: it is the only part here that can break a
        // build in files the reader does not own, so it must not sit under two other lists.
        Move 0 to iShadows
        If (bCancel = False) ;
            Get ShadowCopiesFrom (&asLeaf) (&asWinner) sHome (&asAll) (&asErrFiles) (&aRows) (&iInsGone) to iShadows
        // which DIFFERENT copies add nothing the workspace uses (2026-11-12) - the content line says so
        If (bCancel = False and iShadows > 0) Begin
            Get psTargetPkgFolder of ghoApplication to sInstall
            Get MarkCopiesThatAddNothingUsed (&aRows) (&asAll) sInstall to iSafe
        End
        Move 0 to iLive
        Move 0 to iDormant
        Move (SizeOfArray(aRows) - 1) to iLast
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (aRows[i].eKind = eShadowInstall) Begin
                If (aRows[i].iClass = 0) ;
                    Increment iLive
                Else ;
                    Increment iDormant
            End
        Loop
        If (iLive > 0) Begin
            Writeln channel iCh "*** THE WORKSPACE IS OVERRIDING DATAFLEX SYSTEM FILES ***"
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            Writeln channel iCh "Each file below exists in the workspace under the SAME NAME as one that ships with"
            Writeln channel iCh "DataFlex, and the workspace's copy is the one this build used. That is the most damaging shape of"
            Writeln channel iCh "shadowing, because the errors it causes appear in DataFlex OWN packages - files you did"
            Writeln channel iCh "not write and would never think to suspect."
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            Writeln channel iCh "A real case: a workspace carrying its own 1992 errornum.inc, holding 299 of the 392"
            Writeln channel iCh "DFERR_* constants the installed DataFlex defines. It won, and its #IFDEF guard then"
            Writeln channel iCh "stopped the real one loading at all. The build produced 573 errors, every one of them"
            Writeln channel iCh "pointing at an install file, and the last was an End_Object without Object that read"
            Writeln channel iCh "like a broken view in the application."
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            Writeln channel iCh "Before removing one, check whether it holds anything the installed version does not -"
            Writeln channel iCh "an old copy is usually a strict SUBSET, and then nothing can depend on what it adds."
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            For i from 0 to iLast
                If (aRows[i].eKind = eShadowInstall and aRows[i].iClass = 0) Begin
                    Writeln channel iCh ("=== " + aRows[i].sLeaf + "  (overrides a DataFlex system file) ===")
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  compiled from : " + aRows[i].sPath)
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  shipped file  : " + aRows[i].sShipped)
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  content       : " + (_ContentVerdict(Self, aRows[i])))
                    If (aRows[i].bKept = True) ;
                        Writeln channel iCh "  decision      : KEPT by you - off the board's line until you offer it again"
                End
            Loop
            Writeln channel iCh ""
        End
        /* THE COPIES THIS BUILD NEVER READ - the same name, the same install file, and a listing
           that shows the INSTALLED copy compiling (or the name absent). Harmless today; not for
           ever. Listed apart from the overrides because the two need different sentences: one
           changed this build, the other cannot change any build until it is reached. */
        If (iDormant > 0) Begin
            Writeln channel iCh "*** COPIES OF DATAFLEX SYSTEM FILES THIS BUILD DID NOT READ ***"
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            Writeln channel iCh "Each file below sits in the workspace's source under the same name as one that ships with"
            Writeln channel iCh "DataFlex, but this build read the INSTALLED copy - or never included the name at"
            Writeln channel iCh "all: the folder is off the search path, or nothing Uses it. It compiles nothing"
            Writeln channel iCh "today and wins the day the compiler reaches it, and such a copy is usually years"
            Writeln channel iCh "behind the package it is named after. Renaming it changes nothing this build"
            Writeln channel iCh "compiled; a program this listing does not cover may still reach it on its own build."
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            For i from 0 to iLast
                If (aRows[i].eKind = eShadowInstall and aRows[i].iClass <> 0) Begin
                    Writeln channel iCh ("=== " + aRows[i].sLeaf + "  (a DataFlex system file this build did not read) ===")
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  workspace copy: " + aRows[i].sPath)
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  shipped file  : " + aRows[i].sShipped)
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  content       : " + (_ContentVerdict(Self, aRows[i])))
                    If (aRows[i].bKept = True) ;
                        Writeln channel iCh "  decision      : KEPT by you - off the board's line until you offer it again"
                End
            Loop
            Writeln channel iCh ""
        End
        /* A COPY COMPILED IN PLACE OF THE FILE OF A PACKAGE THAT FAILS (2026-11-12) - the one kind of
           library-file copy listed since 2026-10-05; see FailingPackageCopies. */
        Move 0 to iFail
        For i from 0 to iLast
            If (aRows[i].eKind = eShadowFailingPackage) ;
                Increment iFail
        Loop
        If (iFail > 0) Begin
            Writeln channel iCh "*** COPIES COMPILED IN PLACE OF THE FILE OF A PACKAGE THAT HAS ERRORS ***"
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            Writeln channel iCh "Each file below sits in the workspace's own source under the same name as a file of a"
            Writeln channel iCh "package. This build compiled the workspace's copy in its place, and that package has"
            Writeln channel iCh "errors in this build. The package's other files were written against its own copy, so"
            Writeln channel iCh "the workspace's copy may be what breaks them: a leftover LANGUAGE.PKG gave a package"
            Writeln channel iCh "76 errors that way. The package can also fail for reasons of its own - compare the two"
            Writeln channel iCh "files, or rename the copy and compile again."
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            For i from 0 to iLast
                If (aRows[i].eKind = eShadowFailingPackage) Begin
                    Writeln channel iCh ("=== " + aRows[i].sLeaf + "  (compiled in place of " + aRows[i].sSource + "'s file) ===")
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  compiled from : " + aRows[i].sPath)
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  package file  : " + aRows[i].sShipped)
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  package errors: " + String(aRows[i].iPackageErrors) + " in this build")
                    Writeln channel iCh ("  content       : " + (_ContentVerdict(Self, aRows[i])))
                    If (aRows[i].bKept = True) ;
                        Writeln channel iCh "  decision      : KEPT by you - off the board's line until you offer it again"
                End
            Loop
            Writeln channel iCh ""
        End
        /* ALREADY DEALT WITH, AND THE LISTING HAS NOT CAUGHT UP. These were named by the .prn but
           are no longer on disk - renamed by [Rename them], or removed by hand - so they are not
           listed above. Saying so stops a report run straight after a retire reading as "nothing
           was ever wrong", and names the one thing that makes the difference: another compile. */
        If (iInsGone > 0) Begin
            Writeln channel iCh ("NOTE: " + String(iInsGone) + " overriding copy/copies named by this listing are no longer in the")
            Writeln channel iCh "workspace - already renamed or removed. They are left out above because they cannot"
            Writeln channel iCh "win another build. This listing still predates that change: compile again to confirm."
            Writeln channel iCh ""
        End


        // ---- PART 2: whole library FOLDERS the workspace no longer uses. ----
        If (bCancel = False) ;
            Get _StaleLibraryFolders sHome asListing iCh to iStale

        If (bPanel = True) ;
            Set Title_Text of ghoStatusPanel to ""
        If (bCancel = True) Begin
            Writeln channel iCh ""
            Writeln channel iCh "*** Cancelled by the user - this report is INCOMPLETE. ***"
        End
        Writeln channel iCh ""
        If (iTotal = 0) Begin
            If (iShadows = 0) ;
                Writeln channel iCh "No shadowed files: every package this build included exists in exactly one place."
            Else ;
                Writeln channel iCh "No package is duplicated WITHIN the workspace - but see the copies of shipped files above."
        End
        Else Begin
            Writeln channel iCh "What to do with these - none of it is automatic, and none of it is always right:"
            Writeln channel iCh "  - A leftover copy under an old library folder, shadowing the package the workspace"
            Writeln channel iCh "    now depends on: the copy is what compiles, so fixing the package changes nothing"
            Writeln channel iCh "    until the copy goes."
            Writeln channel iCh "  - A copy carried INSIDE another package: not to be edited there, and a package"
            Writeln channel iCh "    update puts back anything you change. Fix it where that package is maintained,"
            Writeln channel iCh "    then take a newer version of it - or get it to depend on the library rather"
            Writeln channel iCh "    than carry its own copy."
            Writeln channel iCh "  - A deliberate local fork, kept on purpose. Leave it - and consider renaming it,"
            Writeln channel iCh "    so which one the compiler picks stops being a question about folder order."
            Writeln channel iCh ""
        End
        Writeln channel iCh ("Total: " + String(iTotal) + " shadowed file(s), " + String(iStale) + " unused library folder(s).")
        Send rfCloseOutput iCh
        Function_Return (iTotal + iStale)
    End_Function

End_Class
